{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules","id":520134,"title":"M20 House Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-19T16:19:08-07:00","id":520134,"title":"M20 House Rules","content":"Yeah, yeah; I know that the book just got released to the KS Backers. But a key feature of the book is a declared intent to make the game your own; that's one reason why it's chock full of rules variants and options. With that in mind, I'd like to explore house rule ideas above and beyond whan M20 provides. To start off:<br /> <br /> I think the very first house rule I\u2019m going to implement will be to ignore the \u00b13 limit on magical modifiers: if a <i>lot</i> of circumstances are going against you, the difficulty <i>should</i> skyrocket, even if you're casting a one-dot Coincidental Effect; and I want to reward players who put the work in to get the lower difficulties. Besides, it helps offset the quirk in the system where higher-Sphere Effects inherently have more trouble achieving big effects than lower-Sphere Effects, replacing it instead by higher-Sphere Effects tending to layer on the difficulty-reducing modifiers (i.e., putting more effort into it). There will still be a minimum difficulty; but I think I'll base that strictly on vulgarity (4 for Coincidental Effects, 5 for Vulgar Effects, and 6 for Vulgar Effects with Witnesses). <br /> <br /> The second house rule will be to explicitly tie the \u201ctaking extra time\u201d modifiers to your choice of instrument: the more time it takes to use an instrument, the more the difficulty gets reduced. This, as much as a matter of pride, is why a mage might choose to use a slow instrument when an equally suitable fast instrument is available. <br /> <br /> Comments, criticisms, and <i>your own house rules</i> are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T16:44:05-07:00","id":520194,"title":"","content":"Seems reasonable, though I would be very careful not to let those modifiers run out of hand. The power gamer in me would promptly attempt to stack as many positives as possible, then the thematic gamer would slap the power gamer...and attempt to stack as many themes as possible.<br /> <br /> 100% behind taking extra time for profit and glory. Though I might do something fun with options, like taking extra time can reduce paradox, as the Mage's concentrated Will-Over-Time creates a weak Reality Zone.<br /> <br /> Also, this is from another thread, but I'll leave it here as well:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <i>The following hack is intended to add a more gradated feel to a Mage's growth, as well as to allow for bold acts of hubris in novices, and open up plots in the vain of Frankenstein (Etherite novice creates artificial life, with terrible repercussions) and the Sorcerer's Apprentice (Apprentice hermetic attempts to replicate his mentor's spell, with disastrous results).</i><br /> <br /> <b>Reaching And Overreaching</b><br /> Mages can Reach to achieve magical effects above and beyond those their current Spheres would allow. This is a risky endeavor, as without the experience and enlightenment to fully understand their art the Mage's spell will never come out exactly as intended.<ul><li>Reaching is difficult, every dot added increases the difficulty of the final Effect by one. Should the difficulty pass 10 the Mage must expend Quintessence to reduce it to <b>at least</b> 10 otherwise the Effect is impossible to achieve. However, while Quintessence can reduce the difficult down the the base ([4 or 5] + Highest Sphere) it can never reduce it to less than the base difficulty of the Effect.</li> <li>Irregardless of Effect, spells cast through Reaching are always Vulgar. Furthermore, each dot added to achieve the effect tacks an additional point of Paradox onto the spell. Quintessence <i><u>may not</u></i> be spent to negate these additional Paradox points.</li> <li>Succeed or Fail the Storyteller immediately, and unavoidably rolls for Paradox. In addition to all repercussions found on the <i><b>Paradox Backlash Roll chart </b></i>the storyteller may opt to inflict <i>Faults</i> in place of damage, Paradox Flaws, Quiet and other repercussions.</li> <li><i>Faults </i>are flaws in the effect of the spell itself, causing the Effect to come out skewed or even contrary to the original intent. Faults add a new option to the Paradox roll for Reach spells.<ul><li><b>Minor Fault (1-5 Successes)</b>: A small, but inconvenient change in the spell that creates complications for the Mage. Her mystical fire cannot be extinguished by water or dirt, his ray gun emits a powerful magnetic field that bricks all nearby electronics.</li> <li><b>Significant Fault (6-10 Successes)</b>: Something goes seriously wrong with the spell, it may still accomplish its purpose, but not in the way it was intended. A mystical portal through space leads instead to a bizarre Umbral mirror of the intended destination. A transformation curse, while effective, bends the Mage's mind to that of the beast form she has taken.</li> <li><b>Severe Fault (11 - 15 Successes): </b>It's all buggered, the spell goes totally haywire. Even if it somehow manages to achieve the intended effect, it does so with disastrous consequence. An attempt to revive the dead instead summons into the body a cunning, powerful and malicious spirit, well equipped to masquerade as it's familiar host. What should have been a simple rain dance instead conjures an ever growing storm that soon threatens the entire reguin.</li> <li><b>Fuck All (16+ Successes): </b>The Mage has truly, epicly fucked up. If the Fault doesn't kill him outright it will haunt him for the rest of his days. A mad scientist's creature creation proves malignant, and worse, unkillable, it haunts him as a constant shadow through his life.</li> </ul></li> <li>Spells for which the Mage does not meet the requirements can never be declared Rotes, no matter how often the Mage attempts them</li> </ul><b>A Note On Reach: </b>If the character intends to reach more than one or two dots they need to have a justification as to <b>how</b> they can even attempt such a spell (Ex. I witnessed my master perform it as a Rote. I have this ancient Egyptian manuscript detailing the working. It is the logical, upscaled extension of my current practice. My character has been obsessed with this goal ever since he awakened, etc.)<br /> <br /> <b>A Note On Faults: </b>Faults exist as means for the Storyteller to maintain drama and action. As a general rule of thumb a Reach spell should never completely solve a problem. At best it will trade complications, at worst it can create an entirely new, more severe problem. The key here is the focus on what is <b>fun </b>for the players. Inverting every Reach Effect into a terrible punishment isn't fun, and should be reserved only for the most flagrant power gaming. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-20-2015, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T16:55:40-07:00","id":520201,"title":"","content":"I'm dropping the necessity of Certification for some things, mainly weapons. Mainly because I don't see the necessity in making a guy from New York invest two dots of background to legally own a pistol when the character from just across the border in Pennsylvania gets the same thing for free. I get that it models reality more closely (unless your ST is clueless about American firearms law and makes everyone have a &quot;permit&quot;), but it's the kind of small thing that will piss off some of my players, and I expect we'll be touching up character sheets to be &quot;M20-compliant&quot; soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T17:02:41-07:00","id":520208,"title":"","content":"House rule I'm using will be aiming the spell with an actual roll like Perception + Occult or such for Fireball and not Arete. Don't know how you dodge a lightning bolt with ease. Either way, makes Forces almost useless in magic since a single success will beat a Mage. That's such a stupid rule, I don't know why they even added it. Not playing NWoD, why am I rolling to do damage and not to hit?<br /> <br /> Better question is how do you DODGE a freaking curse?<br /> <br /> &quot;Well I felt that damn mage tossing a curse at me so I side step it and dodge the thing! Teach that punk nerd to mess with me!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":2414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","user":"theoutlander523","date":". 05-19-2015, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T17:34:31-07:00","id":520225,"title":"","content":"I think your house rule it's in fact canon in 3\u00ba edition, or at least optional. (You target with Dexterity + the appropriate skill (Occult, Energy Weapons...whatever) and you don't evade curses, because they aren't &quot;energy based attacks&quot;). The old &quot;dodge magick&quot; was just as you described it, an awful and preposterous rule that was added in a very old book: &quot;the Book of Shadows&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't know how you dodge a lightning bolt with ease. </div> </div> </div>Neither do I, but if you can dodge bullets, even at point blank range...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-19-2015, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T18:20:21-07:00","id":520276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=520194#post520194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems reasonable, though I would be very careful not to let those modifiers run out of hand. The power gamer in me would promptly attempt to stack as many positives as possible, then the thematic gamer would slap the power gamer...and attempt to stack as many themes as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not an oversight; that's the intended behavior: the goal is to have a fairly stable set of difficulties (4, 5, or 6, depending on vulgarity), but with high-Sphere requirements and/or troublesome circumstances translating to the mage putting a lot more effort into performing the Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T23:19:06-07:00","id":520532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morimaruvik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=520201#post520201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm dropping the necessity of Certification for some things, mainly weapons. Mainly because I don't see the necessity in making a guy from New York invest two dots of background to legally own a pistol when the character from just across the border in Pennsylvania gets the same thing for free. I get that it models reality more closely (unless your ST is clueless about American firearms law and makes everyone have a &quot;permit&quot;), but it's the kind of small thing that will piss off some of my players, and I expect we'll be touching up character sheets to be &quot;M20-compliant&quot; soon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah 3xp to be able to go hunting or fishing is kind of crazy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T01:09:47-07:00","id":520778,"title":"","content":"Even with an XP cost for Backgrounds staying in M20, it isn't a &quot;must use&quot; rule fairly explicitly. Certification can be a by narrative Background instead of an XP purchased on. Getting a Certification is then only as hard as it is in universe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T04:28:43-07:00","id":521600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=520778#post520778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with an XP cost for Backgrounds staying in M20, it isn't a &quot;must use&quot; rule fairly explicitly. Certification can be a by narrative Background instead of an XP purchased on. Getting a Certification is then only as hard as it is in universe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ok I find &quot;Hunting Liscence&quot; a bit too low a priority for it to be statted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T05:40:09-07:00","id":521690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=520778#post520778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with an XP cost for Backgrounds staying in M20, it isn't a &quot;must use&quot; rule fairly explicitly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, totally. Which is why I don't feel bad at all for dropping it. It's not like dropping, say, Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:42:09-07:00","id":522010,"title":"","content":"I'm still using my &quot;Coincidental, Hidden, Vulgar&quot; variant of Paradox. Basically, in this version, there's no such thing as &quot;vulgar without witnesses.&quot; Coincidental magick is just that -- either something that <i>could</i> happen by the odds, or magick that's wrapped in the local paradigm and thus &quot;possible&quot; by Consensus. Vulgar magick is the impossible, witnessed by Sleepers, who go, &quot;that's impossible!&quot; Hidden is everything in between -- magick that isn't seen by Sleepers. It might be Copperfielding, that wrench in the backpack that wasn't there before, levitating your car out in BFE when no one's around, active telepathy between mages (and/or Night-Folk/Sleepwalkers), etc. It has the same base difficulty as vulgar without witnesses, but doesn't cause auto-paradox -- you only get Paradox on a failure or botch. To compensate, Vulgar magick is even more dangerous based on how many people saw you. A mage automatically gets extra paradox for every factor of ten in people who witnessed your impossibility -- one for 1-9, two for 10+, three for 100+, four for 1000+, and a maximum of five for 10,000+ (after that, the law of diminishing returns shows some mercy on the mage). Failures double this number, and botches start with the doubled nunber and add two for each botch die as usual. It's bad.<br /> <br /> This allows for more of a 1st edition &quot;katanas on rooftops&quot; feel (at least by the art), where magick is fantastic and everywhere, but using it in front of mundanes is an absolute last resort. It also makes the Traditions' position considerably less precarious...which also has the side effect of making the Traditions' devotion to the Sleepers more tenuous. While a lot of Trad mages are still the good guys, there are quite a few (especially Hermetics) who are perfectly happy as secret masters, free to work their magick as they Will, Consensus be damned. Meanwhile, the Technocracy is both a beneficiary and a victim of this effect, able to deploy hypertech freely away from the Masses, but the RDs can do the same with their impossible atavisms. (In my default campaign, this is a result of the Reckoning, which went down differently than Revised canon. Yes, it does have epic, far-reaching consequences when the Awakened realize that Paradox transformed underneath them...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T15:12:17-07:00","id":522586,"title":"","content":"Not exactly a houserule so much as a backpeddle, I plan to entirely ignore the Totem background in M20 in favor of the older one. I do not like the new one one bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T17:17:48-07:00","id":522681,"title":"","content":"Please elaborate: how do they differ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T17:34:57-07:00","id":522716,"title":"","content":"The old Totem rules basically worked like WtA Totems: Totems have a minimum background rating, granting traits and/or powers, as well as a ban; and you could improve it with more points.<br /> <br /> The new Totem rules work very differently, as pointed out in M20, to stress a different relationship. They're more narrative based, with a small set bonus to 1 Ability, Cosmology, and Lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T17:50:33-07:00","id":522728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=522716#post522716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The old Totem rules basically worked like WtA Totems: Totems have a minimum background rating, granting traits and/or powers, as well as a ban; and you could improve it with more points.<br /> <br /> The new Totem rules work very differently, as pointed out in M20, to stress a different relationship. They're more narrative based, with a small set bonus to 1 Ability, Cosmology, and Lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that. I liked the older way better, when you basically made a spirit fragment of the totem that stayed with you, rather than something more far off and out of the way. And of course I liked the more flexible benefits, too. The new way just seems stifling to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T18:30:38-07:00","id":522743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=520225#post520225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your house rule it's in fact canon in 3\u00ba edition, or at least optional. (You target with Dexterity + the appropriate skill (Occult, Energy Weapons...whatever) and you don't evade curses, because they aren't &quot;energy based attacks&quot;). The old &quot;dodge magick&quot; was just as you described it, an awful and preposterous rule that was added in a very old book: &quot;the Book of Shadows&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should have made this an option. It's the one thing that truly irks me about M20.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T19:17:08-07:00","id":522757,"title":"","content":"Having read my way through Chapter 10, and gotten what I hope to be a fair grasp of the casting rules, a somewhat radical hack has come to mind: <b>Completely removing Attributes and Skills</b>. Bear with me. Spheres represent the sum total of all concerted efforts to enforce the Mage's Will on reality, everything from Gregorian Chants and Voodoo ritual to extreme fitness, and social manipulation. Therefore it should be able to model just about any roll.<br /> <br /> The Hack would work thusly. In place of Attributes and Skills a Mage instead has practices (as presented on Page 572). Practices rate 1 - 5 dots, and describe the Mage's talent with a specific branch of her Art. When a Mage wants to perform an action, <b>any action</b>, she uses her Spheres and rolls Arete + Practice. This would, almost unavoidably, result in the abandonment of most of the other systems. All conflicts would be reduced to Arete + Practice vs Arete + Practice (Within reason of course, using Martial Arts to defend against a physical application of Dominance makes perfect sense, High Ritual Magic wouldn't be so reasonable an option).<br /> <br /> A Sample Character Might Look Like This:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Sam The Street Samurai</b><br /> Tradition: Akashic Brotherhood<br /> Arete: 2<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Spheres: Mind 2, Life 2, Forces 1, Matter 2, Spirit 1<br /> Practices: Craftworks 1, Dominion 2, Martial Arts 3, Yoga 1<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Weapons, Armor, Equipment, etc. all become modifiers. A Samurai with a Katana naturally is better at Martial Arts, conversely facing a suit of Full Plate Armor would penalize the Samurai's rolls (as his Paradigm indicates this is an effective defense). The same full plate would offer little help against a ray gun, or physic onslaught.<br /> <br /> Obviously Practices shouldn't be limited to the short list in chapter 10, some of the Secondary Abilities fit quite nicely, and I'd need to figure how to handle sleepers and sleepwalkers (probably allow them access to more mundane Practices, limited to one or two dots). Probably also needs to be an allowance for working within the established Consensus (+1 Die and always Coincidental)<br /> <br /> Perhaps this has been proposed before, even covered in a book, I don't know. But my fondness for dice light gameplay, and simplified systems draws me towards it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-20-2015, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T23:47:40-07:00","id":522974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=522728#post522728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that. I liked the older way better, when you basically made a spirit fragment of the totem that stayed with you, rather than something more far off and out of the way. And of course I liked the more flexible benefits, too. The new way just seems stifling to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise you already had Familiar if you wanted a spirit companion? Totem as it stands is an excellent representation of what actually following a totem is about. It's not about powers, it's about embodying the essence of an idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T01:58:10-07:00","id":523037,"title":"","content":"Well, now that I've had a bit more time to digest the crunch:<br /> <br /> One of the first things I'm going after is the damnable Ability bloat.<br /> <br /> I'm not really too annoyed at the inclusions of Secondaries with a lot of them clearly going after either niche concept specific stuff, or at least specific game tones (Technomagic happy ones esp.).<br /> <br /> However it does seem like the Core Abilities are full of strange redundancies. This is made worse by the introduction of one of my favorite rules from the 20th era books so far regarding the core cWOD system: Well-Skilled Craftsman.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure exactly what I want to mess around with. But I know I want to reduce the numbers. I didn't see the need to separate out Art and Expression, while keeping Leadership (a bunch of the Expression Specialties easily do whatever Leadership is supposed to do). I definitely hate having Brawl, Martial Arts, and Do. MA is getting cut, and Well-Skilled Craftsman being used to gate special maneuvers under Brawl. Do is getting cut (which other splat gets their own super Ability now?). Do will be an Esoterica specialty; whether or not all the basic bonuses stick around or not I'm not sure. But the whole point of the Esoterica Ability (heck High Rituals can go there too...) seems to be a &quot;focus/practice based source of extra cross-Ability specialties.&quot; It also helps make Do more than Brawl+ since it can actually boost other things within its philosophy.<br /> <br /> I'd probably put Animal Ken back in there to replace MA; with Animal Kinship going into Esoterica as well (for practices that do a lot of spiritual animal bonding rather than mundane animal stuff). Ride can go back to being an Animal Ken specialty.<br /> <br /> Another thing that's been bugging me are the splat Affinity Spheres. I get that there's no real &quot;balance&quot; that's needed here. Some groups having a small selection and others having larger ones isn't that big of an issue. The Hermetics being stuck at Forces is a giant WTF considering the number of Houses in previous material that focus on other Spheres.<br /> <br /> I think I either want to drop the splat Affinities as a requirement all together and just have them be suggestions (and then beef out the Hermetics to include at least Mind and Prime), or even them out a bit (put everyone by the Hollowers and Orphans to three of them) and give everyone <i>two</i> specialty Spheres; one free pick and one splat pick. I'm not sure if I want to be mean to the Hollowers and Orphans and leave them with the single any pick, or give them two any picks to stay on par with everyone else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T06:25:35-07:00","id":523121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=522974#post522974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realise you already had Familiar if you wanted a spirit companion? Totem as it stands is an excellent representation of what actually following a totem is about. It's not about powers, it's about embodying the essence of an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm well aware of what options there are, thank you.<br /> <br /> A familiar is more like a bygone retainer than anything else. It also doesn't provide any benefits. The thing I liked about Totem was the combination; there's something different about having a familiar with you in the umbra and having a fragment of a Totem avatar with you.<br /> <br /> And I don't see why getting a capability that's different than dice is against what totem represents; it's an affinity for what the spirit's capable with either way.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:52:10-07:00","id":523189,"title":"","content":"I'm debating the possibility of requiring every Practice to single out one of its associated Abilities as that Practice's <i>Essential Ability</i>: this Ability reflects how well you understand the nuances of your Practice, and serves as a Minimum Ability for all of your Effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:05:27-07:00","id":523436,"title":"","content":"That seems a tad restrictive/just going to have people game the system. If I have to pick one Ability that governs everything I do, why wouldn't drop as many dots into it as I can justify at start?<br /> <br /> It basically screws people wanting to play a young mage learning the ropes (because they have yet another trait capping what they can do), while doing nothing to people playing a mage that's already firmly bought into a given practice (if my Hermetic's Essential Ability was Occult, I'd just start with Occult 3 at a minimum off the bat and have everything covered until I'm working on Arete 4 and a 4th dot in a Sphere, which gives me plenty of time to get Occult 4+ assuming I don't start there anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T14:59:54-07:00","id":523728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523436#post523436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems a tad restrictive/just going to have people game the system. If I have to pick one Ability that governs everything I do, why wouldn't drop as many dots into it as I can justify at start?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if you don't have any Spheres above two dots, there\u2019s no point in raising the Ability in question above two dots? Because you're building to concept instead of building to efficiency? Conversely, why is it a problem if someone with, say, the Practice of Hypereconomics decides to dump a bunch of dots into Finance? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523436#post523436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It basically screws people wanting to play a young mage learning the ropes (because they have yet another trait capping what they can do), while doing nothing to people playing a mage that's already firmly bought into a given practice (if my Hermetic's Essential Ability was Occult, I'd just start with Occult 3 at a minimum off the bat and have everything covered until I'm working on Arete 4 and a 4th dot in a Sphere, which gives me plenty of time to get Occult 4+ assuming I don't start there anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the young mage learning the ropes won't have more than one or two dots in any given Sphere <i>anyway</i>; so only having one or two dots in the Essential Ability isn't a hindrance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T15:30:07-07:00","id":523760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523728#post523728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if you don't have any Spheres above two dots, there\u2019s no point in raising the Ability in question above two dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having it as high as possible at start means I don't have to worry about raising it later when I buy up my actual magical traits. That's what your idea encourages. Picking an Ability and coming up with reasons to start with it at 4-5 so you don't have to worry about not having it cap your magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because you're building to concept instead of building to efficiency? </div> </div> </div>The idea that these are separate is never good from a design perspective. What you make effective, is what you're telling players are the kinds of concepts you consider default. You house rule idea basically says that the default concepts in your game are going to be around people that are highly skilled in at least one Ability that links to their practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conversely, why is it a problem if someone with, say, the Practice of Hypereconomics decides to dump a bunch of dots into Finance? </div> </div> </div>When did I say it was a problem? The problem is <i>forcing</i> them to have at least Finance 3 to cast procedures that use Spheres at 3; even if their knowledge of Finance and how that interacts with their Hypereconomic practice isn't really that important (for example needing a 3rd dot to cast something on someone else doesn't really require a greater understanding of Finance than casting it on yourself, even if the magic requires it, or another example if needing Time 4 to hang the spell that would otherwise only be a 2 dot effect jumps it from needing Finance 2 to Finance 4).<br /> <br /> Yes, characters should have decent investment in the Abilities linked to their practice, and the minimum Ability rating rules are good for helping to enforce the relationship of mundane and magical knowledge. But when you turn it into a mandatory hard cap like that, it gets in the way as much (or more) than it helps anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that the young mage learning the ropes won't have more than one or two dots in any given Sphere <i>anyway</i>; so only having one or two dots in the Essential Ability isn't a hindrance. </div> </div> </div>It's a hindrance in that they have to buy their practice Ability and Arete everytime they want to improve a Sphere that's hit those caps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T16:14:51-07:00","id":523775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523760#post523760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having it as high as possible at start means I don't have to worry about raising it later when I buy up my actual magical traits. That's what your idea encourages. Picking an Ability and coming up with reasons to start with it at 4-5 so you don't have to worry about not having it cap your magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing how this is a problem. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523760#post523760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that these are separate is never good from a design perspective. What you make effective, is what you're telling players are the kinds of concepts you consider default. Your house rule idea basically says that the default concepts in your game are going to be around people that are highly skilled in at least one Ability that links to their practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Again, I'm not seeing the problem. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523760#post523760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is <i>forcing</i> them to have at least Finance 3 to cast procedures that use Spheres at 3; even if their knowledge of Finance and how that interacts with their Hypereconomic practice isn't really that important (for example needing a 3rd dot to cast something on someone else doesn't really require a greater understanding of Finance than casting it on yourself, even if the magic requires it, or another example if needing Time 4 to hang the spell that would otherwise only be a 2 dot effect jumps it from needing Finance 2 to Finance 4).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are a few fringe cases where it might not make sense \u2014 such is <i>always</i> the case when you're attempting to model a complex concept in a way that's playable \u2014 but for the most part, a strong case can be made that an understanding of Finance is <i>essential</i> to being able to properly wield Hypereconomics. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523760#post523760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, characters should have decent investment in the Abilities linked to their practice, and the minimum Ability rating rules are good for helping to enforce the relationship of mundane and magical knowledge. But when you turn it into a mandatory hard cap like that, it gets in the way as much (or more) than it helps anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I think, is <i>very</i> dependent on a given group's style of play. Note that M20 all but suggests this as things stand already, for <i>some</i> Practices: Hypertech comes to mind as an Ability that doesn't particularly serve any purpose <i>other than</i> providing a Minimum Ability rating. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523760#post523760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a hindrance in that they have to buy their practice Ability and Arete everytime they want to improve a Sphere that's hit those caps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how easy it is raise an Ability compared to the difficulty of raising Arete, that's not much of a hindrance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T18:02:50-07:00","id":523820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523775#post523775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not seeing how this is a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're the one putting &quot;concept over efficiency&quot; and then saying that you want to use efficiency to enforce a particular mode of play.<br /> <br /> The problem is that you're adding a rule that doesn't seem at actually add anything to the game if people are already playing under the assumptions you want to play under, but will frustrate people that aren't.<br /> <br /> Which seems the solution is just set your expectations. Not add mechanical kludges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, there are a few fringe cases where it might not make sense \u2014 such is <i>always</i> the case when you're attempting to model a complex concept in a way that's playable \u2014 but for the most part, a strong case can be made that an understanding of Finance is <i>essential</i> to being able to properly wield Hypereconomics. </div> </div> </div>Except the rules as-is don't fall for this by (1) making it optional and (2) have it apply to the application of Abilities as instruments.<br /> <br /> Those factors make sure the rule doesn't get in the way. Yes, technological paradigms (you keep harping on this, but your house rule was phrased for all practices, not just technological ones) are going to be more fringe cases. But more mystic styles are going to be less fringe and more annoying. In your house rule, my PC with Martial Arts 3 as his primary Practice Ability, and Meditation 4, can't use Meditation 4 with a 4th dot Mind effect when using Meditation as his instrument... because he doesn't have Martial Arts 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given how easy it is raise an Ability compared to the difficulty of raising Arete, that's not much of a hindrance. </div> </div> </div>More than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T18:24:32-07:00","id":523824,"title":"","content":"Okay so this is well worn territory I think but as someone who's never actually gotten Mage to the table, does a casting pool of Arete+Sphere break anything? If it does, can you reign it in with the Revised Divided Successes option?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T21:05:23-07:00","id":523962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523820#post523820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're the one putting &quot;concept over efficiency&quot; and then saying that you want to use efficiency to enforce a particular mode of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, my position is that I don't care which way efficiency supposedly drives the players; because in my experience, it's not a big enough factor to worry about. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523820#post523820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that you're adding a rule that doesn't seem at actually add anything to the game if people are already playing under the assumptions you want to play under, but will frustrate people that aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that reasoning, nobody should ever use the Minimum Abilities option; because either the players will already be taking their competence or lack thereof with the Ability into account (in which case imposing a Minimum is pointless) or they won't (in which case imposing the limit will frustrate them). Newsflash: restrictions frustrate players who are restricted by them. A power-gamer who wants to play God (literally) will be frustrated when you tell him that he can't. <i>This isn't a bad thing.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the rules as-is don't fall for this by (1) making it optional and (2) have it apply to the application of Abilities as instruments.<br /> <br /> Those factors make sure the rule doesn't get in the way. Yes, technological paradigms (you keep harping on this, but your house rule was phrased for all practices, not just technological ones) are going to be more fringe cases. But more mystic styles are going to be less fringe and more annoying. In your house rule, my PC with Martial Arts 3 as his primary Practice Ability, and Meditation 4, can't use Meditation 4 with a 4th dot Mind effect when using Meditation as his instrument... because he doesn't have Martial Arts 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>If his Practice is Martial Arts, that's appropriate. If his Practice <i>isn't</i> Martial Arts, then making Martial Arts the Essential Ability isn't appropriate.<br /> <br /> BTW, I wasn't &quot;harping&quot; on the techno paradigms; as you noticed, I had phrased it more generally. It's just that techno-practices are the ones that tend to come to my mind first. (I mention this only because you have a nasty habit of throwing around terms such as this in a way that portrays the guy you're arguing as being unreasonable in some way \u2014 in effect, an ad hominem attack. It's not conducive to the friendly discussions that these forums try to promote, and I wish you'd just stick to arguing the facts and ditch the innuendos.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-22-2015, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T21:34:13-07:00","id":523975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523824#post523824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so this is well worn territory I think but as someone who's never actually gotten Mage to the table, does a casting pool of Arete+Sphere break anything? If it does, can you reign it in with the Revised Divided Successes option?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you get larger casting pools, you're more likely to reach the success thresholds. You can correct this either by pushing those thresholds higher or, as you suggest, by dividing successes among multiple factors \u2014 though the latter only really works if a given Effect <i>has</i> multiple factors; and the more factors you have to divide your successes among, the more important it is to start with a large pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T22:18:53-07:00","id":524002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523824#post523824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so this is well worn territory I think but as someone who's never actually gotten Mage to the table, does a casting pool of Arete+Sphere break anything? If it does, can you reign it in with the Revised Divided Successes option?</div> </div> </div> </div>Arete+Sphere doesn't break anything I can see in M20 that it wouldn't have broken in previous editions.<br /> <br /> Dividing successes isn't just a Revised thing.<br /> <br /> The one thing to be careful with with increasing the dice-pool is the damage that goes with direct Pattern attacks. When 3-4 successes can kill a target, just rolling Arete isn't so bad. If you're looking at Arete + Sphere, and can drop the diff for a big whammy blast, it's makes killing people really easy<br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523962#post523962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that reasoning, nobody should ever use the Minimum Abilities option;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because the actual rules in the book aren't nearly as restrictive as your house rule. Since the RAW are linked to instruments, not practices, it's a situational restriction.<br /> <br /> As well, as an optional rule, yeah, saying your enforcing it or not (which is part of setting expectations) is important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Newsflash: restrictions frustrate players who are restricted by them. A power-gamer who wants to play God (literally) will be frustrated when you tell him that he can't. <i>This isn't a bad thing.</i> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it is a bad thing. This is a game. For fun. You don't get good things by frustrating players with different play styles from your own with house rules on the mechanics. You get good things by heading this off at the pass by discussing expectations before you start play.<br /> <br /> Limitations are a good thing, but they only work when everyone's on the same page. Frustrating a power gamer in your group on purpose isn't good GMing; it's GM-dickery. If they frustrate themselves because they can't get into a satisfactory social contract with the group; that's on them. No RAW or mechanical house rules change that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If his Practice is Martial Arts, that's appropriate. If his Practice <i>isn't</i> Martial Arts, then making Martial Arts the Essential Ability isn't appropriate. </div> </div> </div>Except, as many a Kung Fu movie will tell you, how good your are at hitting people (the Martial Arts Ability) is not actually the pinnacle of Kung Fu (aka Martial Arts as a practice). So no, it is not inherently appropriate that how good you are at hitting things limits your ability to magically meditate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW, I wasn't &quot;harping&quot; on the techno paradigms; as you noticed, I had phrased it more generally. </div> </div> </div>All your examples are techno-practices (and hypereconomics really). Regardless of why, that falls into the category of &quot;harping&quot; if it is coming off to the person you're talking to (me) as a negatively heavy focus. That's what harping means; that you're overly focused on one thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I mention this only because you have a nasty habit of throwing around terms such as this in a way that portrays the guy you're arguing as being unreasonable in some way \u2014 in effect, an ad hominem attack. It's not conducive to the friendly discussions that these forums try to promote, and I wish you'd just stick to arguing the facts and ditch the innuendos.) </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, my favoritest thing ever, when people whine about the tone of a thread/post in the fashion of shitting all over being friendly by making things personal. You know me so well... that you pick the thing that probably gets me in trouble the most when it comes to tone problems in my responses because I find it incredibly unfriendly. Thanks!<br /> <br /> I didn't make an ad hominem attack on you by saying you were harping on something. It's not innuendo; it is my direct impression of your posts. So stick to arguing the facts. If you feel that my comment about your focus on hypereconomics isn't fair, talk about that, or acknowledge that and start talking about other practices. You could also... not respond to criticism about your ideas by being defensive and dismissive of it. You do want to hear it don't you? If you don't find merit in a criticism, why engage? If you're engaging, why dismiss any elaboration on things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T23:20:53-07:00","id":524057,"title":"","content":"The only house rule I'm going with is the one where you do a shot for each point of paradox you earn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T08:28:34-07:00","id":524465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523824#post523824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so this is well worn territory I think but as someone who's never actually gotten Mage to the table, does a casting pool of Arete+Sphere break anything? If it does, can you reign it in with the Revised Divided Successes option?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do this, I recommend following the example of Dark Ages: Mage and make damage levels equal to number of successes on an Arete + Sphere roll. In M20, each success inflicts roughly 2 levels of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 05-22-2015, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T09:35:39-07:00","id":524519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=524465#post524465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do this, I recommend following the example of Dark Ages: Mage and make damage levels equal to number of successes on an Arete + Sphere roll. In M20, each success inflicts roughly 2 levels of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm doing a similar model, but it's less potent than you think. Consider you need to roll 2 successes before even counting the damage.<br /> Here's my houserules. Some are old and independent of which wod splat we're playing, made more to speed things up than anything else.<br /> 1) Everybody important soaks lethal like bashing. NO ONE soaks Agg without equipment and specific powers for it.<br /> 2) Dealing Agg damage is the exclusive realm of quintessence-infused attacks (and non-chargen powers for other splats). Generally any source of agg damage is halved compared to canon.<br /> 3) Evading or Parrying attacks is reflexive, not a separate action. Reply attacks no longer exist. If everybody's feeling like it, Clash may be used (when two people attack each other on the same initiative...instead of two attack-defense pairs, it's just one attack against the other, winner hits by the success threshold)<br /> 4) Spellcasting roll is Arete+Avatar<br /> 5) Everybody starts with Avatar 1, and raising Avatar during chargen is done with almost the same cost and restrictions as Arete. Avatar may not be raised with XP, though every character will have a fair chance of gaining it over time. (expect 2s and 3s by the end of a few stories)<br /> 6) Standard spellcasting difficulty is 6(coincidental), 7(unwitnessed vulgar) or 8(vulgar with witnesses).<br /> a) The final difficulty modifier is still +-3, but only the final modifier. If something gives you -8 and events also bring a +7, you get a -1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T09:53:50-07:00","id":524556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=524465#post524465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you do this, I recommend following the example of Dark Ages: Mage and make damage levels equal to number of successes on an Arete + Sphere roll. In M20, each success inflicts roughly 2 levels of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. I also recommend making magickal soak a relatively easy thing <i>a la</i> Mage: the Awakening (where <i>every</i> Sphere has an Armor rote at Sphere rank 2, though that's a little far for Ascension IMO). If you roll Arete + Sphere and inflict 2 damage per success, it gets pretty crazy, pretty fast -- especially with Forces and its auto-damage level (which I also apply to soak, BTW). Combat mages become walking tanks, and the already crazy ICBM (Inter-Continental Ballistic Magick) ritual effect turns into a nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T12:11:06-07:00","id":526905,"title":"","content":"My house rules involve inverting the difficulties between Coincidental and Vulgar Magick, and having the universe discourage Vulgar Magic with Paradox and Unbelief. It should be <i>more</i> difficult to make your Paradigm blend in with Consensual Reality, not <i>less</i>. Vulgar w/o Witnesses is an annoying sub-category which can go away. <br /> <br /> Also, dice for casting equals your Arete + your Avatar rating. Your Avatar rating equals 1/2 your Willpower rating, round down. <br /> <br /> Also, I'd like to come up with a way to allow mages to cast over their Sphere Limits, at the cost of things going horribly wrong. &quot;The Sorcerer's Apprentice Effect&quot;, if you will. <br /> <br /> Something has to be done about the Ability bloat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I'd like to simplify how Arete is done in regards to xp. You can buy up Arete with bonus points at character creation to 3 as usual. But from then on, your XP purchases should focus on Spheres, If you attempt to buy up a Sphere over your Arete, you go on a Seeking. At the end, you roll your current Arete versus current Arete +1, and if you win, your Arete goes up. If you lose, you have to wait until your next Sphere hits your Arete rating. Once all Spheres are at your Arete rating, you go up automatically. This changes once you hit Arete 5, but I'm working out the details on that. I don't want Arete to be an xp sink; I want the players out there getting into trouble and making things go <b>BOOM! </b>around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:50:17-07:00","id":527063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=526905#post526905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My house rules involve inverting the difficulties between Coincidental and Vulgar Magick, and having the universe discourage Vulgar Magic with Paradox and Unbelief. It should be <i>more</i> difficult to make your Paradigm blend in with Consensual Reality, not <i>less</i>. Vulgar w/o Witnesses is an annoying sub-category which can go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. And given that Coincidental has benefits that Vulgar lacks (i.e., much less Paradox), it's not like you're working extra hard to get nothing in return. I also agree about ditching the distinction between Vulgar and Vulgar With Witnesses as far as the difficulty is concerned \u2014 though I'd keep it, maybe even enhance it, when calculating how much Paradox you get. Something where the bigger the audience is, the nastier Paradox gets. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=526905#post526905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, dice for casting equals your Arete + your Avatar rating. Your Avatar rating equals 1/2 your Willpower rating, round down.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;equals&quot;, or &quot;starts at&quot;? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=526905#post526905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'd like to come up with a way to allow mages to cast over their Sphere Limits, at the cost of things going horribly wrong. &amp;quot;The Sorcerer's Apprentice Effect&amp;quot;, if you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any thoughts on PenDragon's first post in this thread?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=526905#post526905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something has to be done about the Ability bloat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I'd like to simplify how Arete is done in regards to xp. You can buy up Arete with bonus points at character creation to 3 as usual. But from then on, your XP purchases should focus on Spheres, If you attempt to buy up a Sphere over your Arete, you go on a Seeking. At the end, you roll your current Arete versus current Arete +1, and if you win, your Arete goes up. If you lose, you have to wait until your next Sphere hits your Arete rating. Once all Spheres are at your Arete rating, you go up automatically. This changes once you hit Arete 5, but I'm working out the details on that. I don't want Arete to be an xp sink; I want the players out there getting into trouble and making things go <b>BOOM! </b>around them.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Mage: the Awakening</b> introduced the concept of \u201cArcane Experience\u201d, a second type of experience that you earn by investigating supernatural phenomena but limited in terms of what they can be spent on (primarily Gnosis, that game's counterpart to Arete \u2014 which explains why \u201cinvestigating the supernatural\u201d is the primary way to earn it). Arcane Experience is earned <i>in addition to</i> regular experience, so your regular xp rewards are freed up for other uses. <br /> <br /> For <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, I'd change the means of earning it: Gnosis is all about attaining a deeper understanding of the world's mysteries; Arete is about being excellent. Select the earning conditions properly, and you'll get a double whammy: not only will regular xp be freed up for other uses, but Arcane Experience will be most effectively earned by going out there, getting into trouble, and making things go <b>BOOM!</b> around them. IIRC, the <b>Mage Translation Guide</b> has some advice on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:07:42-07:00","id":527129,"title":"","content":"Certification is definitely gone. Sinking four starting background points just for a medical license is ridiculously overcosted.<br /> <br /> I was hoping we might see some sort of standardization among basic Ability sets between 20th edition games, with Hobby Talent/Professional Skill/Expert Knowledge being used to cut out the bloat, and just focusing on the handful of important secondary skills in each game, but no such luck. Technology really made more sense as a Knowledge. &gt;.&lt; Back to a knowledge it is.<br /> <br /> I'd say I'd start with just using the Abilities from Vampire 20th and then working from there.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts is gone; we don't need Brawl+. Why the Hell take Brawl?<br /> <br /> Animal Kinship as distinct from Animal Ken is fine.<br /> Blatancy isn't happening.<br /> Carousing is a drop.<br /> Do I'll keep.<br /> Flying is really just an Athletics subset.<br /> High Ritual seems more like a focus of Etiquette, Occult, or proper Academics: Sociology specialty.<br /> Lucid Dreaming is fine.<br /> Search is going away.<br /> Seduction I'd drop; you can get the effect from Empathy and Subterfuge.<br /> Acrobatics is good.<br /> Archery is good; it's never really been close to Firearms or Athletics for my tastes.<br /> Biotech is really a Science specialty.<br /> Energy Weapons is best done as a Firearms specialty.<br /> Hyper Tech and Jet Pack are both fine.<br /> Riding I might keep as a skill.<br /> Pilot skill seems to be dropped from the book.<br /> Torture is something I've thought best role-played.<br /> Area Knowledge I don't like and rarely use even in games that feature it.<br /> Belief Systems is a whole slew of different skills, but could mostly be covered purely by Academics.<br /> Cryptography is fine.<br /> Demolitions is fine.<br /> Finance is fine.<br /> Lore/R&amp;D data means I'm really not sure what you are trying to accomplish with Occult any more. If Esoterica covers occult practices, and Lore/R&amp;D covers knowledge of other supernaturals, what is left, and why is Occult even useful any more?<br /> Media is fine.<br /> Pharmacopeia/Poisons is just Medicine skill, flat-out. Redundant Redundancy Department of Redundant Redundancy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T06:50:08-07:00","id":527624,"title":"","content":"I was planning on solving the ability bloat problem by giving them extra freebie points to spend on them. Perhaps 5 extra points, What do you think about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T08:35:01-07:00","id":527717,"title":"","content":"Giving extra points does mean it will be easier for specialized characters to outstrip more general characters. It's an okay solution if it's even bloat, but for uneven bloat it means characters with fewer required abilities for their specialization will get a leg up.<br /> <br /> I find it easier just to take the Red Pen to things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:00:20-07:00","id":527937,"title":"","content":"I think it helps to start by just treating the whole Secondary section as Hobby/Professional/Expert examples and never require them for play.<br /> <br /> Though I've been thinking of combining Hypertech and Esoterica to basically be the same with with a different name depending on your focus. The point of both is how well you understand mystic/hypertech principles and can apply them to actions even if they aren't casting an effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:04:22-07:00","id":527945,"title":"","content":"Some are worth toddling out on their own; they work for very limited concepts which means they shouldn't necessarily be on the sheet but have a place in the game.<br /> <br /> Others though, no.<br /> <br /> Blatancy for example (which I feel is in there just as much as a historical curio as anything) reminds me of the Intrigue secondary ability found in some WoD games, and I take mostly the same issue with it: to me, it feels like trying to get the dice to play the game for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T15:33:27-07:00","id":528150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=527937#post527937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it helps to start by just treating the whole Secondary section as Hobby/Professional/Expert examples and never require them for play.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent, yes. That said, Hobby Talents, Professional Skills, and Expert Knowledges are subject to the Well-Skilled Craftsman option, allowing you to make a jack-of-all-trades (Professional Skill + Well-Skilled Craftsman option) or a polymath (Expert Knowledge + Well-Skilled Craftsman option). With that in mind, I think my preferred approach here would be to introduce a counterpoint to Well-Skilled Craftsman, namely an option that explicitly lets you single out a Specialty of another Ability and take it as an Ability in its own right; then I'd go through the various Secondary Abilities and recast as many of them as possible as Specialties of the core Abilities. For instance, Flying would become a Specialty of Athletics, and Hypertech would become a Specialty of Esoterica. <br /> <br /> The ones I'd keep separate would be ones that cut across several core Abilities (e.g., High Ritual), ones that don't seem to fit as Specialties of <i>any</i> core Abilities, and ones that are essentially reskins of existing Abilities but applied to something else (Archery vs. Firearms; Riding or Pilot vs. Drive). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I've been thinking of combining Hypertech and Esoterica to basically be the same with with a different name depending on your focus. The point of both is how well you understand mystic/hypertech principles and can apply them to actions even if they aren't casting an effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. We've got a number of Abilities with dual names depending on whether you're dealing with A mystic mindset or a technological one; to me, it looks like Esoterica and Hypertech is the same sort of thing. Indeed, the only reason I can think of for keeping them separate is that, as written, Hypertech is capped by Technology while Esoterica has no comparable restriction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-25-2015, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T15:39:34-07:00","id":528152,"title":"","content":"Esoterica can be capped by Occult. There, I fixed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T16:28:27-07:00","id":528213,"title":"","content":"Satyros himself said in the facebook group that occultism could be considered an specialty of academics which I agree. As for fitting the other abilities as specialties I like it, I will talk with my players and see what they think. If you guys wouldn't mind sharing what you did at the end I would appreciate it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 05-25-2015, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T16:33:40-07:00","id":528215,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about it for a few days now, and I believe I'm just going to count the secondary abilities as specialties. It seems like the easiest method across the board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T16:43:09-07:00","id":528220,"title":"","content":"When I can, I'm going to sit down with a list of the Core and Secondary Abilities and map out which Core Ability I think each Secondary Ability could be a Specialty of. Unless someone else beats me to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:04:11-07:00","id":528535,"title":"","content":"Paradox house-rule: as written, Paradox Backlashes work a lot like they do in Revised, except that you don't get Paradox Burn reductions when you cross the 10-point and 20-point thresholds. On the one hand, this avoids the oddity of an 11-point Backlash being less painful than a 10-point Backlash (I'd much rather deal with 1L rather than 10B); OTOH, if you take Lethal damage <i>at all</i>, you'll take at least 11 points of it \u2014 and Aggravated damage is even worse: I know that a 21-point discharge <i>should</i> be the end of the character; but the fact that you take 21 points of Aggravated damage kind of renders the other effects of such a backlash moot. <br /> <br /> So, my house rule. The damage done by a Backlash can be one of the following:<br /> \u2022 1B per point discharged;<br /> \u2022 1L per two points discharged, rounding up;<br /> \u2022 1A per three points or fraction thereof discharged.<br /> <br /> The player can usually choose which of these he wants, though large Backlashes start taking options off the table: if more than 10 points are discharged, you can't take the Bashing option; and if more than 20 points are discharged, you must take the Aggravated option. <br /> <br /> This way, there are no odd breakpoints, <i>and</i> it's possible to live long enough to suffer the other consequences of a huge backlash: 7 points of Aggravated damage will hurt; but you <i>just might</i> survive it. <br /> <br /> I'm also debating whether or not it should be soakable; and if so, what you should use to soak it. I'm thinking right now of making it soakable via your Avatar rating, <i>maybe</i> with the possibility of Prime-based anti-Backlash armoring Effects as well. I do <i>not</i> think it should be soakable via Stamina; this is magick ripping away at the very core of your being, not a cut or a burn (despite the name). <br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh, and a second house rule: you can choose to intensify the side effects of a Backlash in exchange for mitigating or even negating the Burn. I'm still working on the exchange rates; but I'm thinking that some sort of conversion rate between Bashing damage and Quiet might be in order, for Backlashes that are associated with less tangible Effects. This would be <i>in addition to</i> whatever side effects the Backlash would normally cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-26-2015, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:12:39-07:00","id":528543,"title":"","content":"Yeah, soaking via Avatar rating (or perhaps with Arete + Avatar) sounds like a good idea. Magical soak for magical damage. Or maybe you could use Prime to create a sort of &quot;Paradox Soak Armor&quot; rote. I mean, we have Prime 5 that nullifies Paradox, so perhaps you could have a Prime 4 effect that partially protects against Paradox backlash. Or perhaps Prime 4 + Life 3 (or 4).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T00:48:44-07:00","id":528627,"title":"","content":"1) I'd personally round down instead of up for the exchange rates. It's already really deadly. Having a small zone of not instant death for higher levels of backlash (6 Agg at 20 is still extremely nasty, and 21-23 is still in the narrative &quot;might survive&quot; zone).<br /> <br /> 2) I'd avoid using Avatar myself. Avatar is already a bit much of a &quot;must take a few dots&quot; Background; and one that is very difficult to raise in play. What about having it be Stamina (if you can naturally soak the type of damage without magic, so bashing only for most mages) + Prime? It's easier than tracking a spell you're going to have on all the time if you're going to be racking up lots of Paradox to just use Prime as the rating. You can even let Avatar sneak in by letting players spend Quintessence to reduce the soak difficulty; so a powerful Avatar can help you avoid exploding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T03:57:14-07:00","id":528697,"title":"","content":"I'd avoid Paradox as damage entirely and go for Paradox as &quot;fucks your life up utterly&quot;. It's more fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T04:11:25-07:00","id":528706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=528627#post528627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I'd personally round down instead of up for the exchange rates. It's already really deadly. Having a small zone of not instant death for higher levels of backlash (6 Agg at 20 is still extremely nasty, and 21-23 is still in the narrative &quot;might survive&quot; zone).</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. And it simplifies the written rule, too; good all around. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=528627#post528627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I'd avoid using Avatar myself. Avatar is already a bit much of a &quot;must take a few dots&quot; Background; and one that is very difficult to raise in play. What about having it be Stamina (if you can naturally soak the type of damage without magic, so bashing only for most mages) + Prime? It's easier than tracking a spell you're going to have on all the time if you're going to be racking up lots of Paradox to just use Prime as the rating. You can even let Avatar sneak in by letting players spend Quintessence to reduce the soak difficulty; so a powerful Avatar can help you avoid exploding.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point is to <i>not</i> use Stamina to soak; if you must use an Attribute for it, I'd rather use one of the Mental ones, as they're more suitable to the archetypal magic user. <br /> <br /> That said, I would likely be pairing this house rule with one that changes Avatar into a standalone Advantage, like Willpower or Arete; to me, it's too central, conceptually as well as mechanically, to being a Mage to be treated as a Background. <i>That</i> hack potentially would change how difficult it is to raise, too. <br /> <br /> Alternately, I could introduce a <i>new</i> trait, one that gets used to soak Paradox and perhaps to facilitate countermagic. Establish a sort of triad of mystical traits (Arete for Effect-shaping rolls, Avatar for how much \u201cjuice\u201d you have, and this third one for how resistant you are to the supernatural).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T05:51:57-07:00","id":528733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=528220#post528220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I can, I'm going to sit down with a list of the Core and Secondary Abilities and map out which Core Ability I think each Secondary Ability could be a Specialty of. Unless someone else beats me to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>These aren't perfect and are subject to revision/debate, but at present:<br /> <br /> Animal Kinship -&gt; Empathy or Survival<br /> Blatancy -&gt; Subterfuge<br /> Carousing -&gt; Leadership or Etiquette<br /> Do -&gt; Martial Arts<br /> Flying -&gt; Athletics<br /> High Ritual -&gt; Etiquette, Esoterica or Occult<br /> Lucid Dreaming -&gt; Meditation<br /> Search -&gt; Alertness or Investigation<br /> Seduction -&gt; Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Acrobatics -&gt; Athletics<br /> Archery -&gt; Athletics<br /> Biotech -&gt; Technology or Medicine<br /> Energy Weapons -&gt; Firearms<br /> Hypertech -&gt; Technology<br /> Jetpack -&gt; Technology<br /> Riding -&gt; Athletics<br /> Torture -&gt; Intimidation<br /> <br /> Area Knowledge -&gt; completely unrequired, IMO, covered by backstory<br /> Belief Systems -&gt; Academics, Esoterica or Occult<br /> Cryptography -&gt; Research, Enigmas or Investigation<br /> Demolitions -&gt; Science<br /> Finance -&gt; Law<br /> Lore/R&amp;D -&gt; Occult<br /> Media -&gt; Politics<br /> Pharmacopia/Poisons -&gt; Medicine<br /> <br /> Very much just a quick first pass. Multiple entries suggest different slants/approaches depending on character. Several of these are pretty iffy; I just really dislike the idea of a ton of secondary abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T08:10:08-07:00","id":528785,"title":"","content":"I'd consider dividing Specialties into two types: Fields and Techniques. Academics, Crafts, and their like would have Fields that define what the scope of the Ability covers: pick one when you take the Ability; pick up others later to expand your scope. All Abilities would have Techniques, which would be specific <i>uses</i> of the Ability that you're especially capable of. <br /> <br /> Jet Pack shouldn't be a Technology Specialty, any more than Drive should be. Actially, Drive should be expanded to be more like Science or Crafts, with Field Specialties including Bikes, Cars, Trucks, Trains, Boats, Ships, Jet Packs, Helicopters\u2026 As with Crafts, if you want to be able to operate more than one kind of vehicle, you need to take more than one Specialty. Similarly, Firearms and Melee could potentially benefit from Fields: pistols, rifles, and bazookas are very different things, as are knives, mauls, and nunchucks. <br /> <br /> I'd like to restructure the way Esoterica works, too: I want every Field Specialty to have an associated Ability that serves as a cap: for instance, Yoga would be capped by Meditation; Tantra would be capped by Athletics; Herbalism would be capped by Medicine; Kabbalah would be capped by Academics (Jewish Theology); Astrology would be capped by Science (Astronomy); Alchemy would be capped by Science (Chemistry); and so on. I would try <i>not</i> to use Occult as the cap for any of them, though it might turn out to be unavoidable. <br /> <br /> With this in place, Do and Hypertech could become regular Specialties of Esoterica, respectively capped by Martial Arts and Technology; and I'd move Hypermathematics over from Science to Esoterica (or fold it into Numerology), with Science (Mathematics) serving as its cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T08:21:26-07:00","id":528792,"title":"","content":"I totally get what you're saying, but it conflicts with my one-page-two-max-per-character-sheet KISS doctrine. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T09:45:18-07:00","id":528865,"title":"","content":"Oh? How so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T09:49:02-07:00","id":528868,"title":"","content":"Mainly in that it's more complicated. Not a criticism, just an observation. You have abilities, then specialisations with techniques and fields; I'd prefer just abilities with specialisations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T09:56:31-07:00","id":528900,"title":"","content":"But you've <i>already</i> got that complexity; I just assigned a formal name to the way that Crafts and Academics work, and suggested that it can exist alongside the default way that Specialties work (e.g., \u201cResearch\u201d can be a Specialty for Academics and/or Science). The rest is simply applying it more broadly, so as to avoid having to make up a slew of Secondary Abilities such as Biker, Boats, Jet Pack, or Pilot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T09:59:39-07:00","id":528902,"title":"","content":"I obviously misread, then. If you're saying the same thing I was with extra names (and some disagreement about what maps to what), ok. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:25:22-07:00","id":529427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=527063#post527063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;equals&quot;, or &quot;starts at&quot;?<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on PenDragon's first post in this thread?<br /> <br /> <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> introduced the concept of \u201cArcane Experience\u201d, a second type of experience that you earn by investigating supernatural phenomena but limited in terms of what they can be spent on (primarily Gnosis, that game's counterpart to Arete \u2014 which explains why \u201cinvestigating the supernatural\u201d is the primary way to earn it). Arcane Experience is earned <i>in addition to</i> regular experience, so your regular xp rewards are freed up for other uses.<br /> <br /> For <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, I'd change the means of earning it: Gnosis is all about attaining a deeper understanding of the world's mysteries; Arete is about being excellent. Select the earning conditions properly, and you'll get a double whammy: not only will regular xp be freed up for other uses, but Arcane Experience will be most effectively earned by going out there, getting into trouble, and making things go <b>BOOM!</b> around them. IIRC, the <b>Mage Translation Guide</b> has some advice on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking &quot;equals&quot;, but maybe &quot;starts at&quot; would be the better way to go. <br /> <br /> Quite a few thoughts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Arcane Experience&quot; is probably the way to go. Have to dig out the Translation Guide. <br /> <br /> I was also thinking about getting rid of the Archmage problem with borrowing from Matt Sheppard's &quot;Superhero Mages&quot; idea: let the Arete (player's option) give a multiply successes option. For example, if your mage has Arete 6, that can multiply the successes rolled by x2. And the multiplier goes up. Of course, doing that is Vulgar as hell, and if you botch, you get the multiplier in Paradox. But if you've gotta risk it...<br /> <br /> And last but not least, I have an idea for condensing Spheres. Slide the lion's share of Entropy into Time, and mush Prime and Spirit together. That gives 7 Spheres, Easier to make a well-rounded Mage from the get-go, And it doesn't risk Time being kinda soft while Entropy risks becoming a Swiss-Army knife. Push the damaging aspects of Entropy into the appropriate other Spheres. Let the Pattern Spheres make &quot;something out of nothing&quot; without needing Prime 2. Everything gets beefed up. <br /> <br /> Plus, I think I can build a campaign around the idea of 9 Spheres shrinking down into 7...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:29:01-07:00","id":529429,"title":"","content":"Also: Limit Dodging to coincidental Effects. If you're going Vulgar, the target better have some sort of countermagic or they're screwed. The technocracy spends all that time being Coincidental, then the mages they're hunting should get something out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T18:32:58-07:00","id":529480,"title":"","content":"I'm willing to say you can dodge up to a point, but some things you are SOL. Fire balls, lightning, etcetera, you can dodge, but it will be a lot like dodging a bullet: very high difficulty. Direct curses, transformations, anything that targets the mind or soul, or anything that targets the body directly, too bad. You will need a counter for those.<br /> <br /> Some things, like say dodging out of the way of an Entropy effect make the bridge underneath collapse might be possible, but only if you have somewhere to actually dodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T13:29:22-07:00","id":530262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=529480#post529480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm willing to say you can dodge up to a point, but some things you are SOL. Fire balls, lightning, etcetera, you can dodge, but it will be a lot like dodging a bullet: very high difficulty. Direct curses, transformations, anything that targets the mind or soul, or anything that targets the body directly, too bad. You will need a counter for those.<br /> <br /> Some things, like say dodging out of the way of an Entropy effect make the bridge underneath collapse might be possible, but only if you have somewhere to actually dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I agree, and I'd rule that having a bridge collapse is coincidental in the World of Darkness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T16:33:59-07:00","id":530394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=523037#post523037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now that I've had a bit more time to digest the crunch:<br /> <br /> One of the first things I'm going after is the damnable Ability bloat.<br /> <br /> I'm not really too annoyed at the inclusions of Secondaries with a lot of them clearly going after either niche concept specific stuff, or at least specific game tones (Technomagic happy ones esp.).<br /> <br /> However it does seem like the Core Abilities are full of strange redundancies. This is made worse by the introduction of one of my favorite rules from the 20th era books so far regarding the core cWOD system: Well-Skilled Craftsman.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure exactly what I want to mess around with. But I know I want to reduce the numbers. I didn't see the need to separate out Art and Expression, while keeping Leadership (a bunch of the Expression Specialties easily do whatever Leadership is supposed to do). I definitely hate having Brawl, Martial Arts, and Do. MA is getting cut, and Well-Skilled Craftsman being used to gate special maneuvers under Brawl. Do is getting cut (which other splat gets their own super Ability now?). Do will be an Esoterica specialty; whether or not all the basic bonuses stick around or not I'm not sure. But the whole point of the Esoterica Ability (heck High Rituals can go there too...) seems to be a &quot;focus/practice based source of extra cross-Ability specialties.&quot; It also helps make Do more than Brawl+ since it can actually boost other things within its philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Art, at least as far as non-written works, a function of Crafts? The past few iterations of the 20th anniversary rules tend to point that way, just as surely as Technology is a Knowledge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T17:01:30-07:00","id":530412,"title":"","content":"Art could be collapsed (partially back) into Crafts; especially with the Well-Skilled Craftsman rules. Though I can see an argument for Art being a much more important separation in Mage compared to Vampire or Werewolf.<br /> <br /> I'm not really hard set on any of the particular possible ways to reduce the Ability bloat besides Brawl/MA/Do. Just in general there's too much of it.<br /> <br /> And Technology has flirted in different editions as either a Skill or a Knowledge.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm a fan of dumping Computers and replacing it with Technology; modern technology is far too digital to bother separating them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T17:29:20-07:00","id":530434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=530412#post530412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Art could be collapsed (partially back) into Crafts; especially with the Well-Skilled Craftsman rules. Though I can see an argument for Art being a much more important separation in Mage compared to Vampire or Werewolf.<br /> <br /> I'm not really hard set on any of the particular possible ways to reduce the Ability bloat besides Brawl/MA/Do. Just in general there's too much of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even though I tend to be distant from Mage, the Do Arms Abilities post on FB way back when made me turn my head sideways at all of the secondaries and odd redundancies. I guess it feeds on the same dread I have at the prospect of Kailindo and/or Klaive Dueling coming back as Skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Technology has flirted in different editions as either a Skill or a Knowledge. </div> </div> </div>But in V20 and W20, it's a Knowledge. I'm not seeing too much of a need to change that, is my point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I'm a fan of dumping Computers and replacing it with Technology; modern technology is far too digital to bother separating them. </div> </div> </div>Or clearly denote Computers as the programming Ability, and Technology as the hardware Ability. Programming languages might not fit quite so well under the Languages merit, but then I suppose that you can just have them as DAV20 Crafts-style fields of expertise for Technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T00:47:51-07:00","id":530731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=530434#post530434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though I tend to be distant from Mage, the Do Arms Abilities post on FB way back when made me turn my head sideways at all of the secondaries and odd redundancies. I guess it feeds on the same dread I have at the prospect of Kailindo and/or Klaive Dueling coming back as Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least Kailindo or Klaive Dueling have a balance to them. Both offer access to a specific unique set of maneuvers (though really Klaive Dueling is often a stretch to make this worth it), but can be very limited in how useful they are (both are very obvious and supernatural, making that a problem on its own). Kalindo relies on shifting, which is fairly draining. Klaive Dueling relies on having a Klaive and it even being useful for what you're doing. Basically, neither really replaces the basic combat Abilities, because you're going to have Athletics/Brawl/Melee for all the times they aren't going to apply.<br /> <br /> Do, on the other hand, completely replaces Brawl and MA (with the small exception that you can't use Do with Dirty Fighting maneuvers but Do is better anyway). There's no reason to buy either once you have access to Do (hell you can't buy MA once you have Do).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in V20 and W20, it's a Knowledge. I'm not seeing too much of a need to change that, is my point. </div> </div> </div>Oh, I like it better there as well, but it isn't like having it as a Skill is out of the blue.<br /> <br /> I figure M20 put it as a Skill mostly because the Knowledges are very packed and not easy to pick out ones to cut; and they wanted symmetry on the sheet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or clearly denote Computers as the programming Ability, and Technology as the hardware Ability. Programming languages might not fit quite so well under the Languages merit, but then I suppose that you can just have them as DAV20 Crafts-style fields of expertise for Technology. </div> </div> </div>I'd actually move most coding into Science (we do call the field Computer Science and all that), Esoterica/Hypertech (for Science! coding instead of regular coding) or Enigmas (assuming Cryptology gets put in there instead of as a secondary for when that might be necessary) if I was dumping Computers. A skill just for coding is actually a bit silly. Programming languages aren't really appropriate as full languages any more than having to take mathematics as a language to do calculus proofs outloud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T02:32:27-07:00","id":530801,"title":"","content":"I disagree on Computers, I think they're justified being their own skill. If nothing else, wouldn't it be just an enormous middle finger to the Virtual Adepts to marginalize their signature activity as being &quot;just a branch of Technology&quot; or something. Moreover, you use Computer for things like Hacking, and the idea that it's regularly used for programming is implied. Finally, using a computer is, in fact, a skill (or set of Knowledge in this case) that you need to develop separate from anything else. It requires a different skill set to do. An Etherite that's seventy years old might be absolutely killer with both Science and Technology, but be completely stumped by the non-intuitive nature of computers. Or just look at your average old person try to make the infernal device work. In the same way that you need Brawl in order to know how to fight hand to hand beyond the limb flailing phase, so to do you need Computer to use one at all beyond the keyboard hitting phase.<br /> <br /> Here's another point, if we're saying that one Ability is &quot;basically&quot; like another, why don't we go further with that. Why not fold Brawl into Athletics? Or Science and Technology into Academics? Or hell, why don't we just roll all Abilities into their appropriate Attributes, since we're simplifying? Instead of marking someone's individual skills, why don't we just make solid Attribute rolls for anything and everything?<br /> <br /> It's not that I don't agree that the Abilities have become bloated. But the entire reason we have them in the first place is to let us play characters with varied and specific skill sets. Do we really need Computer when we have Science? Strictly speaking no, but we have it as a separate skill regardless because in real life it is its own discipline. And when you devote time to learning this specific skill, that's time you're not devoting to learning something else. If we go too far with collapsing Abilities into other Abilities, we'll prune the system to oblivion and be stuck with characters that are generic and boring. Characters who can all do everything because their Abilities do everything. And we can't rely on Specialties, because some skills are broad enough to have many areas of expertise within them. We'd have Specialties within Specialties!<br /> <br /> I'm sorry for ranting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T07:47:46-07:00","id":531010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=530801#post530801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree on Computers, I think they're justified being their own skill. If nothing else, wouldn't it be just an enormous middle finger to the Virtual Adepts to marginalize their signature activity as being &quot;just a branch of Technology&quot; or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's completely in line with their presentation in M20 as moving past their &quot;Virtual life is freedom, all digital all the time,&quot; 90s cyberpunk thing and having them grow more integrated with the physical world as the Internet and things like AR have become more prominent.<br /> <br /> The problem with computers is that computers are in <i>everything</i> and have grown to be extremely basic in terms of operation. Using a computer today, vs. 20 years ago, is a massively different thing.<br /> <br /> Think about all of these things which have computers in them: cars, TVs, video game consoles, phones, watches, exercise equipment, fridges, thermostats, alarm clocks, etc.<br /> <br /> We're in a digital age. We stick computers in everything. Which basically means Computers is really solely for coding (which is kind of silly, there are programming languages designed for grade schoolers now).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moreover, you use Computer for things like Hacking, and the idea that it's regularly used for programming is implied. </div> </div> </div>Hacking, IRL, is and has never been highly based on coding. Hacking is a mixture of social engineering, brute force computations (aka just hitting run on a program), knowledge of exploits, and knowing the hacker subculture. Raw coding is basically the least important skill to hacking these days (and it has never been that important compared to knowing what to do with it). This is best represented as a series of Abilities, not one just for hacking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, using a computer is, in fact, a skill (or set of Knowledge in this case) that you need to develop separate from anything else. It requires a different skill set to do. An Etherite that's seventy years old might be absolutely killer with both Science and Technology, but be completely stumped by the non-intuitive nature of computers. </div> </div> </div>And and old enough one might be baffle by an automatic transmission too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T11:48:17-07:00","id":531175,"title":"","content":"Sorry, time issues forced me to cut this into two:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=530801#post530801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another point, if we're saying that one Ability is &quot;basically&quot; like another, why don't we go further with that. Why not fold Brawl into Athletics? Or Science and Technology into Academics? Or hell, why don't we just roll all Abilities into their appropriate Attributes, since we're simplifying? Instead of marking someone's individual skills, why don't we just make solid Attribute rolls for anything and everything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Slippery slopes require more than just saying they could happen to be valid points.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I've seen people hack the ST system to completely remove Abilities. The nWOD presented this in one of their system hacking focused books as well. So that's not a bad thing, or inherently wrong; it also doesn't prove one must go to that extreme.<br /> <br /> It is very simple to look at the Ability list and set up a series of heuristics that end up reducing the total Ability count with a reasoned approach that doesn't sacrifice the role Abilities play in describing your character. For example:<br /> <br /> 1) If two Abilities have nearly identical functions and any differences can be maintained using existing other rules, or there is not a significant risk in dropping the differences, combine them (ex: Brawl and Martial Arts, Esoterica and Hypertech).<br /> 2) If one Ability's practical applications accomplish everything another Ability's uses accomplish (or worse and more) combine them (ex: Do and Martial Arts, Expression and Leadership), or if one Ability's practical applications are covered completely by two (or more) other Abilities combine it into those (ex: Computers into Technology and Science, Research into appropriate Knowledges governing that topic).<br /> 3) Only maintain a separation of &quot;theory focused&quot; Abilities and &quot;application focused&quot; Abilities (ex: Occult vs. Esoterica) if both Abilities have significant impact in play.<br /> 4) When it doubt, keep Abilities that have a strong conceptual niche (ex: Rules 1-3 could make a case to eliminate Medicine in Investigation for diagnostics, Science for theory/lab work, and Empathy or Technology for treatment depending on the nature of the condition, but Medicine is a strong enough niche role for healer-types to keep).<br /> 5) Maintain Ability list symmetry; all categories should have the same number of core traits. If Knowledges has 11 Abilities and Talents only has 8, it has a negative impact on prioritization during character creation.<br /> <br /> Yes, there's plenty of subjective calls in there, but you can follow that, cull out 1 or 2 Abilities per category, and not negatively impact characterization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the entire reason we have them in the first place is to let us play characters with varied and specific skill sets. </div> </div> </div>Multiple variations of the ST systems have set Ability/Skill lists, often with less of them (Exalted has 25, nWOD has 24), and no built in assumption of expansion-as-needed (Secondaries or the Hobby/Professional/Expert traits), and still manage to accomplish this goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do we really need Computer when we have Science? Strictly speaking no, but we have it as a separate skill regardless because in real life it is its own discipline. </div> </div> </div>You can say that about any science... why aren't biology, chemistry, physics, and mathematics at a minimum separate Abilities, as all are their own real life disciplines? Computers isn't there because information theory and programming design isn't a science, but because of (1) legacy issues regarding the relative specialization of computer use from 20+ years ago and (2) as something the follows #4 on my list above in the game creator's minds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And when you devote time to learning this specific skill, that's time you're not devoting to learning something else. </div> </div> </div>True, but ultimately this doesn't make a solid point. Training up Science instead of Technology is time spent on one specific thing over another regardless of there being 24 Abilities, 33 Abilities, or 60 Abilities. This has no baring on the number of them. It's also not spending time improving Attributes that could likely increase your facility with multiple Abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we go too far with collapsing Abilities into other Abilities, we'll prune the system to oblivion and be stuck with characters that are generic and boring. </div> </div> </div>Conversely, if we bloat Abilities too far, they simply become unwieldy and frustrating for trying to make sheets that reflect specific concepts because more dots get tied up in basic proficiencies for the concept and don't leave room for personalizing them. It does not take large numbers to accomplish lots of combinations. Just think for a moment how many different permutations you can actually get out of V20's Ability options at creation without freebies. So that's 13/9/5 in to three categories of 10. Just for the tertiary alone, there are five spreads (all1s, 1/1/1/2, 1/2/2, 1/1/3, 2/3). Which works out to over 2,500 different unique combinations of your tertiary Abilities alone. You can make 2,500 characters and never repeat the same tertiary Ability assignments once with 30 Abilities. The idea that we're at risk of losing uniqueness by cutting out a few doesn't work; and M20 starts at 33.<br /> <br /> If I want to make an Akashic that started as a street brawler making their money in underground fights and was good, but came to an epiphany that their life style was destructive and sought to find a positive outlet for their passion through studying formal martial arts with a strong philosophic bent, before Awakening and becoming an Akashic...<br /> <br /> In the current rules I should take Brawl, Martial Arts, Do (and probably a few other things), and the first two should have at least a reasonable investment for the concept (lets say 3/3/2). Of course, I'm never going to use Brawl or MA, because I have Do and Do is far superior even if I start with a bit less of it.<br /> <br /> If we use my house rule presented earlier, I can just take Brawl (with an appropriate MA specialy via Well-Skilled Craftmen) at 3, and Esoterica with a Do specialty at 2 for the same level of competence. Now I have three more dots to make sure that I can flush out my character with other traits to be less cookie-cutter Martial Arts fighter.<br /> <br /> Or to reverse your slippery slope on you: Why should the game stop at 33 Abilities, why not 66? or 330? The more Abilities, the more ways to make unique combinations, the less generic and boring, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T12:52:43-07:00","id":531211,"title":"","content":"The main argument I can see for keeping Brawl and Martial Arts as separate things is that Brawl is a Talent while Martial Arts is a Skill; and I'd only consider that to be a significant argument to the extent that there's some sort of <i>game system</i> distinction between Talents and Skills. The main argument I see for combining them is that I can't think of anything that Brawl lets you do that Martial Arts doesn't let you do just as well or better. As things stand, I can't think of any reason why anyone would take dots in both, except maybe to reflect a character's backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T13:37:32-07:00","id":531235,"title":"","content":"Hell, why not fold Melee and Brawl together? Why not give everyone Martial Arts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T14:24:09-07:00","id":531258,"title":"","content":"Honestly? I've been debating something like that. Remember my earlier suggestion about dividing Specialties into two types (Fields and Techniques)? I'm thhinking of maybe dropping Martial Arts and giving Melee a set of Fields based on different kinds of weapons \u2014 including an \u201cunarmed\u201d option. <br /> <br /> As for Brawl vs Martial Arts/Melee: I forget; what does M20 have to say about using Abilities when you don't have any dots in them? If M20 doesn't have anything like this at the moment (I can't check at the moment), I'm thinking of implementing something like the nWoD's \u201cunskilled use\u201d rules, with Talents being usable without any drawbacks if you lack training, Skills being usable at a mild increase to the difficulty, and Knowledges either featuring a significant difficulty boost or maybe even some sort of \u201cminimum proficiency\u201d system, where lacking sufficient dots for a given task means that you automatically fail (if you don't have any training in Science, you're not going to be able to <i>understand</i> the clash between Quantum Mechanics and Relativity, let alone <i>resolve</i> it. Just to pick one rather extreme example.) With such a system in place, a distinction between a Brawl Talent and a Melee (Unarmed) Skill still makes sense, despite the overlap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T14:49:02-07:00","id":531270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=531211#post531211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main argument I can see for keeping Brawl and Martial Arts as separate things is that Brawl is a Talent while Martial Arts is a Skill; and I'd only consider that to be a significant argument to the extent that there's some sort of <i>game system</i> distinction between Talents and Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that the distinction between Talents and Skills, mechanically, is the untrained penalty. Since Martial Arts maneuvers require at least one dot in MA or Do before you can use them, you never roll them untrained.<br /> <br /> If you have Brawl 0 and MA 0, you have access to the same basic close combat maneuvers, though technically if you pick Brawl they are base difficulty as a Talent, but if you pick MA you roll at +1 difficulty. But you'd never opt mechanically to take a +1 for no actual reason. If you have Brawl &gt; 0 and MA 0, there's no reason to ever roll MA because you can't attempt the MA maneuvers anyway even with a +1 difficulty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main argument I see for combining them is that I can't think of anything that Brawl lets you do that Martial Arts doesn't let you do just as well or better. As things stand, I can't think of any reason why anyone would take dots in both, except maybe to reflect a character's backstory. </div> </div> </div>Well, technically, Brawl's big thing is that at Brawl 3 you get <b>all</b> the Dirty Fighting maneuvers if your concept backs it up (and why would you make a character with Brawl that can't back that up if that's the only thing Brawl is best at?), but there's only 8 of them. Going with Martial Arts gets you 2 moves per dot. This means you can never get all of them (though most are also limited by style specialty). So Brawl 3 grants you access to 8 extra tricks, while MA 3 only gets you 6 extra tricks.<br /> <br /> Of course, the MA moves are generally superior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=531235#post531235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, why not fold Melee and Brawl together? Why not give everyone Martial Arts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've considered having it just be &quot;close combat&quot; as one big Skill. It's very tempting in the nWOD (esp. 2e) where Brawl might as well be called Grapple + whatever you buy with Merits to make punching people worth it. The cWOD combat systems generally give enough for Brawl/MA/Do to do separate from Melee that a pure unarmed character isn't going to feel like a chump next to someone with a blade.<br /> <br /> If I was aiming to trim the M20 skills below 10 a category, it would be tempting. But since I'm not, it doesn't feel necessary.<br /> <br /> As for why not give everyone MA? Well then it's just which name to call it isn't? I personally prefer the more general of the two when merging things, so Specialties can be more evocative. Brawl lets you have specialties like &quot;Back Alley Beatdowns,&quot; that don't really sound right as a Martial Arts specialty, while still sounding good with Specialties that would more naturally overlap (ex: Drunken Master).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T15:16:06-07:00","id":531278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=531270#post531270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this is that the distinction between Talents and Skills, mechanically, is the untrained penalty. Since Martial Arts maneuvers require at least one dot in MA or Do before you can use them, you never roll them untrained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please provide a page reference. What you say makes sense (though it seems a bit harsh to flat-out forbid the untrained use of Skills); but I can't find the rule anywhere in M20. Hopefully, I just overlooked it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I found it in V20, at the top of the Skill and Knowledge lists, respectively. It does not appear in the corresponding places in M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-28-2015, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:32:10-07:00","id":531413,"title":"","content":"Hrm. Yeah. I'm so used to that (It's in Mage Rev. too) that I didn't even think to check on it. I can't seem to find it.<br /> <br /> So Brawl 0 and MA 0 are the same.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T10:26:07-07:00","id":534577,"title":"","content":"In a game I wrote, all forms of combat just fall under one skill, called Violence. I think it works out, personally.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> I really don't understand the point of keeping the shitty version of Occult. Did they not realize they are allowed to change/redefine skills? No, Esoterica is fucking gone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T13:56:55-07:00","id":534792,"title":"","content":"Not quite the way I'd phrase it; but yeah: I don't see much point in an Ability dedicated to comprehending the misinformation that mystically-inclined Sleepers labor under; and as much as I love Esoterica, I wouldn't mind it being called Occult instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T01:06:58-07:00","id":535349,"title":"","content":"Based on talk in the Entropy Thread I started, I'm going to change the Sphere to &quot;Fate&quot; and let all other Entropy and Death related effects fall under their respective spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T09:34:20-07:00","id":537138,"title":"","content":"My proposed HR Mage Abilities for non-technocrats:<br /> <br /> |<b>Talent</b>|<b>Skill</b>|<b>Knowledge</b>|<br /> |Alertness|Crafts|Academics|<br /> |Athletics|Drive|Computer|<br /> |Brawl|Esoterica|Cosmology|<br /> |Empathy|Etiquette|Enigmas|<br /> |Expression|Firearms|Investigation|<br /> |Intuition|Meditation|Law|<br /> |Intimidation|Melee|Medicine|<br /> |Leadership|Performance|Occult|<br /> |Streetwise|Stealth|Science|<br /> |Subterfuge|Survival|Technology|<br /> |(Hobby Talent)|(Professional Skill)|(Expert Knowledge)|<br /> <br /> This just seems to fall more in-line with the other 20th anniversary lines.<br /> <br /> I picked <b>Intuition</b> over <b>Awareness</b> as I feel Mages are essentially human and shouldn't have access to special senses except through sphere effects. I'm using the write-up from Mage 1st for the Talent. <b>Intuition</b> is more about instincts and &quot;gut feelings&quot; than awareness of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> I like the <b>Esoterica</b> concept, but since it seems to be more about the practices than the knowledge, I moved it over to a skill. My technocracy alternative to this skill might be <b>Hypertech</b>. I dropped <b>Larceny</b> from the original list that I made before the Mage 20 Quick-Start was released to include Esoterica.<br /> <br /> I moved <b>Technology</b> back under Knowledge, like V20 and W20 has it.<br /> <br /> For the Secondary Abilities, I'm pretty much going to make them specialties of other Abilities. As a Storyteller, I'm just not going to call for a <b>Pharmacopoeia</b> or <b>High Ritual</b> roll during a game. I'm going to ask for <b>Medicine</b> or <b>Science</b> or <b>Etiquette</b>, something I can see on the main sheet. <br /> <br /> <b>Do</b> might be the only exception to this preference for no secondary abilities. I'm definitely using the Eight Limbs of Do. My Mage games will have simplified combat and won't be using the maneuvers for <b>Martial Arts</b> and <b>Do</b> present in M20. If I want to feature violence (or the players do), I'll use something like WOD: Combat for everyone. I'm thinking the basic Do abilities (lethal attack, hardened defense, well-trained) presented in the TB:AkBro (p. 63), will be enough to make Do a special ability without it unbalancing combat or other parts of the game.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Jason, the Storyteller<br /> -<br /> &quot;Old dreams become new again in the spring. This is where the nightmares are.&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1357-storyteller31","name":"Storyteller31","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T10:04:30-07:00","id":537169,"title":"","content":"I entirely disagree with removing Awareness for Mages. By their very nature, Mages are Aware of the way things truly work in the world (Even if filtered through their group's lens). I've always been a proponent of it working BETTER for them than anyone else with it (which M20 seems to allow for, since they gain auto-aura perception now) as it's really the only thing about them that IS supernatural without a Sphere.<br /> <br /> The rest of your ideas seem good, though I'm uncertain on removing maneuvers for MA and Do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T11:57:37-07:00","id":537272,"title":"","content":"The distinction between Talent, Skill, and Knowledge isn't about whether it's about the practices rather than the facts; it's solely about how hard it is to try if you don't have any training or education. Esoterica is very much the sort of thing where if you don't know anything about what you're doing, you're going to fall flat on your face; that makes it a Knowledge. <br /> <br /> I missed that bit about mages now having an aura auto-perception; could you provide a page reference, please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T12:36:34-07:00","id":537318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=537272#post537272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I missed that bit about mages now having an aura auto-perception; could you provide a page reference, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>M20, p. 276, Awareness &quot;At lower levels, this Talent grants a nebulous perception of uncanny phenomena; higher ratings in the Trait reveal auras, expose the secretive Night-Folk, and open your eyes to the spiritual Periphery.&quot; &quot;\u2022\u2022\u2022 Skillful: You can see auras, and you understand what those colors mean.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not auto, but I know I'd let characters with at least one dot try and suss out someone's aura. This is one of the reasons I personally prefer Intuition to Awareness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Jason, the Storyteller<br /> -<br /> &quot;Old dreams become new again in the spring. This is where the nightmares are.&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1357-storyteller31","name":"Storyteller31","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T12:36:40-07:00","id":537319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=537272#post537272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The distinction between Talent, Skill, and Knowledge isn't about whether it's about the practices rather than the facts; it's solely about how hard it is to try if you don't have any training or education. Esoterica is very much the sort of thing where if you don't know anything about what you're doing, you're going to fall flat on your face; that makes it a Knowledge.<br /> <br /> I missed that bit about mages now having an aura auto-perception; could you provide a page reference, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the writeup of Awareness itself, page 276.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">At lower levels, this Talent grants a nebulous perception of<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">uncanny phenomena; higher ratings in the Trait reveal auras,<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">expose the secretive Night-Folk, and open your eyes to the<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">spiritual Periphery.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> It also specifically references the aura table, which makes it clear that isn't just flavor:<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">For a reference chart of aura colors and textures, see<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Chapter Ten, </b><span style=\"color:#4A1A71\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>(p.507)</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T13:59:16-07:00","id":537413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller31</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=537138#post537138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I picked <b>Intuition</b> over <b>Awareness</b> as I feel Mages are essentially human and shouldn't have access to special senses except through sphere effects. I'm using the write-up from Mage 1st for the Talent. <b>Intuition</b> is more about instincts and &quot;gut feelings&quot; than awareness of the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awareness isn't unique to Mage, or Awakened. In the World of Darkness, it's an ability (and Ability) any human can learn to use. I even use it as an Instrument in my Psychic Focus (as presented in another thread).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T16:58:18-07:00","id":537516,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to note that Awareness was introduced in Vampire later than in Mage <hr /><br /> Some thoughts:<br /> <br /> The difficulties for Mind are seriously wrong... If I understand correctly, using a Mind 3 Coincidental spell on a single mage with a very normal Willpower of 7 it's difficulty 10 (Will + 3), but casting it on TWO mages, <i>that's difficulty 6</i> (Sphere + 3) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That can't be right. I propose to either ditch this rule, or use the highest Willpower (+3, if appropriate) of the group as difficulty.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I dislike the fact that the &quot;Night-Folk&quot; not only can counter the magick of mages (while most of them can't counter their own magical powers), but are better at countermagic than mages...<br /> <br /> Giving countermagic with an Attribute + Ability or Willpower (whichever is higher, for vampires, spirits and many others...), it's totally overkill. The average neonate vampire can easily have 5-6 dots of &quot;Arete&quot; worth of countermagic this way. Any weak, newbie, supernatural being can have stronger countermagick than most mages (As I understand that only a few, rare and powerfull, mages have Arete 6+)<br /> <br /> Also, the rule that makes the roll harder against mages with Arete 7+ , it's laughable. Those mages aren't &quot;powerfull mages&quot;, but &quot;very powerful, and incredibly rare&quot;, to the point that dificulty 6 it's the average difficulty for countermagick for no-mages (while mages roll at dif. 7)<br /> <br /> This it's limited by not working against direct magical assaults, like plasma canons (that can be evaded)<br /> <br /> I'm pondering to either ignore this not-optional rule (it doesn't say to be optional), or maybe to make the &quot;supernatural counterspelling roll&quot; harder. The roll may have a difficulty of the mage's Arete +3 (5-7 for average mages), or maybe to divide the successes by 2 (like old Taumaturgy countermagic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-02-2015, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T07:07:02-07:00","id":538244,"title":"","content":"Well, I think the book says that is not Wits + Occult or Willpower/Rage/Glamour/Whatever but Wits + Occult capped by Willpower/Rage/Glamour/Whatever. That's different.<br /> <br /> And it's not only limited with not working against direct magical assaults as it also doesn't work against indirect magickal effects, so at the end it only does against effects that directly affect their Patterns. Add to that they need to specifically have the Occult knowledge to countermagick, an ability that not all the other Night-Folk are going to have. And then you can use the whole optional limit about them not even being able to counter unless said Night-Folk got some sort of magical knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T07:22:22-07:00","id":538253,"title":"","content":"That's true. I stand corrected.<br /> <br /> Still I don't like it a bit. Mages also have trouble at counterspelling indirect magickal assaults (they do it at dif. 8), albeit they're still superior in this aspect. And the so called &quot;cap&quot; isn't much of a cap when it's tied to a cheap Trait like Willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> at the end it only does against effects that directly affect their Patterns </div> </div> </div>It actually works against any magick that it's not &quot;direct damage&quot;, or &quot;focused through violence&quot;, or &quot;indirect&quot;. That includes many overt manipulations, not only direct Pattern manipulations. For instance, slowing them with Time wouldn't do, not with their level of counterspelling.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this rule was added only to make the Lawn Chair rote more difficult...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-03-2015, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T07:36:06-07:00","id":538286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=538253#post538253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It actually works against any magick that it's not &quot;direct damage&quot;, or &quot;focused through violence&quot;, or &quot;indirect&quot;. That includes many overt manipulations, not only direct Pattern manipulations. For instance, slowing them with Time wouldn't do, not with their level of counterspelling.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this rule was added only to make the Lawn Chair rote more difficult...</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but still as I said it needs an specific ability for it to work and as the book says it can't be used to avoid having a wall falling in your face or your bank account from being hacked, so I think is mostly fair. But it is true that for the ones who have Willpower to cap the pool (vampires, demons, hunters, wraiths...) it seems a bit too cheap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T07:40:17-07:00","id":538291,"title":"","content":"I have this idea: why not use Mage Lore + Wits, instead of Occult.<br /> This way, it's still possible, but it's justified (and capped) by a much rarer form of Knowledge. The character needs to truly &quot;understand&quot; True Magick before using it's innate magickal powers as a bulwark against it's effects, and not many of the Night-Folk understand it to that level.<br /> <br /> This way , the average cub can't counter magick, but an elder (or any supernatural that has taken time to<i> understand</i> its enemies) may counter all but the most potent of mages (or spells).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:17:33-07:00","id":542761,"title":"","content":"TBH, this rule seems to assume the Night-Folk encountered will be NPCs. In which case, it often benefits the story to make it harder to just turn them into a lawn chair (or whatever). It means mage PCs have to think more creatively, instead of just hurling fireballs. But different games have different crossover rules, so if you wanted to, you could use those rules instead. In V20, for instance, vampires must have Thaumaturgy to resist True Magick, and they roll Wits + Occult (difficulty 6).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:37:34-07:00","id":542781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=538291#post538291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this idea: why not use Mage Lore + Wits, instead of Occult.<br /> This way, it's still possible, but it's justified (and capped) by a much rarer form of Knowledge. The character needs to truly &quot;understand&quot; True Magick before using it's innate magickal powers as a bulwark against it's effects, and not many of the Night-Folk understand it to that level.<br /> <br /> This way , the average cub can't counter magick, but an elder (or any supernatural that has taken time to<i> understand</i> its enemies) may counter all but the most potent of mages (or spells).</div> </div> </div> </div>Lore Abilities, as Secondaries, aren't for every game. Also, there are lots of reality-warping threats in other games; Werewolf, for example, has Triatic Spirits, most notably Nexus Crawlers, Stasis Vectors and Great Vortices, that can all alter existence directly. Viskr Faction Ananasi also have their own exclusive category of rites for this purpose, and the Rite of Weaving is capable of a wide array of broad effects, much as magick is, only requiring a great deal more time and much more likely to go awry. Changeling Wyrd cantrips also work by inviting in something alien to the world in order to alter it, and of course, there are those beings in the Dreaming that are less affected by Banality than the surroundings are from their presence. The basic concept isn't really so unknown to the other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:24:53-07:00","id":542984,"title":"","content":"Let me think. So you think that werewolves should be able to easily resist magick in Mage (as Occult is a common Trait) because they have experience with Nexus Crawlers and such...<br /> <br /> Even when they can't realy counter the effects of Nexus Crawlers in their game.. .<br /> <br /> So, You think that I should let the furries resist magick with Occult because they have experience being unable to resist similar powers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /><br /> Now, since M20 its a Mage book, not a Werewolf book, I think it's perfectly alright to force the furries to use an ability that they can have, since they're playing by Mage's rule. A Trait that isn't so common and easy to get as Occult or Rage.<br /> <br /> Do you have some real sugerence on this?. Do you think that it's perfectly fair to the mages to be unable to affect werewolves with direct magical alterations?<br /> <br /> Even when they can resist and/or evade many, if not most, direct or indirect magics (as bridges falling can be evaded too, by RAW). On top of their total superiority in physical prowess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-06-2015, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:12:19-07:00","id":543426,"title":"","content":"The problem with all this is that Wits and Occult, as common, traits have no default rating. Assuming every night-folk has decent ratings in both and their relevant capping traits is overstating how hard they are to deal with magically. Though it is worth acknowledging that some night-folk are going to be very hard to effect with the M20 rules as written if their concepts happen to align with what's in the rules.<br /> <br /> For example, a Ragabash Homid would have to put a lot into Rage or Gnosis before they're countering anything. An Ahroun Lupus just needs the Wits + Occult ratings.<br /> <br /> Of course, the whole thing seems like it was really just done because for so long mages have been seen as so overwhelming powerful in crossover as most supernaturals have no defense against magic.<br /> <br /> I do think that it could use some tweaking, but I'd only really be worried about that for crossover games. In a pure mage game, night-folk are as good as basic countermagic as the ST wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T22:19:27-07:00","id":543475,"title":"","content":"Here's a request for the other House Rules folks here, anyone willing/able to create a modify-able version of the character sheet in the M20 book? ie. Say I want to replace Occult with Finance, there's a handy dandy word document that I can modify, pdf and then print off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T02:21:03-07:00","id":543647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with all this is that Wits and Occult, as common, traits have no default rating. Assuming every night-folk has decent ratings in both and their relevant capping traits is overstating how hard they are to deal with magically. Though it is worth acknowledging that some night-folk are going to be very hard to effect with the M20 rules as written if their concepts happen to align with what's in the rules.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I do think that it could use some tweaking, but I'd only really be worried about that for crossover games. In a pure mage game, night-folk are as good as basic countermagic as the ST wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I can agree on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:24:19-07:00","id":544141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=543475#post543475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a request for the other House Rules folks here, anyone willing/able to create a modify-able version of the character sheet in the M20 book? ie. Say I want to replace Occult with Finance, there's a handy dandy word document that I can modify, pdf and then print off?</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked Mr. Gone for a M20 sheet with all abilities blank so you can customize them for your chronicle. No commitment or eta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Jason, the Storyteller<br /> -<br /> &quot;Old dreams become new again in the spring. This is where the nightmares are.&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1357-storyteller31","name":"Storyteller31","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T21:33:41-07:00","id":544769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=522728#post522728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that. I liked the older way better, when you basically made a spirit fragment of the totem that stayed with you, rather than something more far off and out of the way. And of course I liked the more flexible benefits, too. The new way just seems stifling to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:15:55-07:00","id":550789,"title":"","content":"Ok, on to new house Rules: I was thinking of how to solve the attack pool issue for &quot;aimed&quot; attacks i.e. Forces3 or Matter 3/Prime 2.<br /> <br /> Why not use Willpower? Magic is controlled by the Mage's will. It starts out at 5 dots, and never goes beyond 10. It doesn't rely on &quot;optimizing&quot; something specific that may not fit the character's concept like Wits+Occult or Perception+Athletics. It could reach 10 dice fairly easily, but players who use Life+Connections attacks won't be penalized for not having Will 10. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T18:39:26-07:00","id":550966,"title":"","content":"Well, IF the Storyteller it's careful on how much Willpower will allow the players to have, it's not bad. Problem with Willpower it's that's a little too cheap (as you start with 5, and one can easily raise it with freebies).<br /> <br /> I think the roll should be Appropriate Attribute + Appropriate Skill (Appropriate being defined by Focus), but that can be somewhat complicated, as needs to be solved in the fly. Willpower it's easier in that sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:56:50-07:00","id":551015,"title":"","content":"Here's the Houserules I've been using for my campaign so far.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Mage House Rules</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Character Creation</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">PC\u2019s start with Arete 3, 9 dots of Spheres, and 1 dot of Avatar.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Affinity Sphere: Pick your own.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Martial Arts:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Every dot of Martial arts must be accompanied with at least 1 dot in the following Abilities: Academics, Medicine, Enigmas, Art, Craft, Meditation, Stealth, Esoterica (Yoga, Tai\u2019chi) These dots must be spread out, only 1 ability counts for each dot.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ability Changes</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The following Abilities may be substituted on your character sheet or added to it. All other secondary abilities do not exist in my game.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">(Talent)</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Animal Kinship,</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">(Skill)</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Do, Archery, Riding,*Quick Draw </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">(Knowledge)</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pilot, Hypertech</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Quickdraw</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: Every dot adds 1 to your initiative for the purpose of drawing and firing a gun in combat. If using the bonus you MUST fire a gun. Can only be used with pistol sized guns.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hypertech:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">This ability functionally works as &quot;Occult&quot; for Technomancers, allowing the identification of supernatural phenomena and explanation of it, through a Technomatic paradigm. You still need awareness to detect such things, but your Mage can identify things such as Ghosts and what they are weak too, by explaining it through some form of psuedoscience. It's also used for handling and understanding wonders and instruments of a technological nature.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A note about Esoterica</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: You may be wondering what this skill is. It\u2019s for being able to perform occult style practices. \u201cHerbalism\u201d, \u201cDemonology\u201d, \u201cHigh Magick\u201d, and the like are examples of Esoterica.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A note on Specialties:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Some abilities require a \u201cfocus\u201d to be used. These abilities can contain many focuses. The Abilities which require them are: Crafts, Art, Science, Esoterica. Additional focuses, however, may be purchased for 4xp, regardless of the number of dots in the ability.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Rule of 10: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Any action involving an ability or attribute rated at 4+ dice allows you to count 10\u2019s as two successes. All Arete rolls automatically count 10's as two successes.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">How can I take Multiple Actions with Magick?</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Life 3: Speed your body\u2019s Reflexes up, Maximum 3 actions around.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mind 2: Speed Synaptic functions, Maximum 2 actions around.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Time 3: Speed self up, no limit on actions.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Correspondence 3: Limited, must be the same exact action, max 5.<br /> <br /> 2 actions a round remains coincidental, 3 actions and above becomes Vulgar.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirit Magick</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirit 1: See and Talk to Spirits and Ghosts.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirit 2: Call Spirits and Ghosts to you.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirit 3: Give orders to Spirits and Ghosts, limited.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirit 4: Command/Dominate Spirit and Ghosts.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T22:37:19-07:00","id":551133,"title":"","content":"If Arete automatically counts 10s as 2 successes... what do Sphere Specialties do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T02:37:29-07:00","id":551211,"title":"","content":"I'm using the same house rules as I did in my revised Ed games. Using the Minor spheres means you roll so sphere plus ar\u00eate on your magic rolls, using a major sphere means you roll ar\u00eate alone.<br /> <br /> Mages suffer one paradox point per dot of the highest sphere used in the effect for vulgar Magic (plus one extra point if there are witnesses) but can 'soak' paradox with ar\u00eate; mages are free to spend quintessence and willpower in this roll, difficulty is 6 (as with all non sphere rolls where a player rolls ar\u00eate in my game).<br /> <br /> Counter magic on effects that influence a Mage can be performed without any spheres using an ar\u00eate roll of difficulty 6 (in most cases) but this only counters magic that is being done or which has been done on said Mage (if the Magic effects multiple people then the counter magic only negates the magic done on the Mage who counters it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","user":"Dream_Walker","date":". 06-13-2015, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:52:25-07:00","id":551357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=551133#post551133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Arete automatically counts 10s as 2 successes... what do Sphere Specialties do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm most likely just not going to use them. No one has an Arete of 4 yet, so I have some time. I might allow it to give an extra die on Arete rolls instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","user":"Orphan81","date":". 06-12-2015, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T15:10:00-07:00","id":554908,"title":"","content":"I've always thought Avatar was too integral as a Background, and encourages min-maxing. I considered having it as a ten-dot Advantage like Arete and Willpower, but realised it would overlap too much with the former. My house rule, then, would be to do away with the Avatar Background altogether and have its mechanics absorbed by Arete. You can channel as many points of Quintessence per turn as you have Arete, then. A simple fix, and a fairer solution, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T13:33:36-07:00","id":555996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=554908#post554908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought Avatar was too integral as a Background, and encourages min-maxing. I considered having it as a ten-dot Advantage like Arete and Willpower, but realised it would overlap too much with the former. My house rule, then, would be to do away with the Avatar Background altogether and have its mechanics absorbed by Arete. You can channel as many points of Quintessence per turn as you have Arete, then. A simple fix, and a fairer solution, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was working on a set of house rules about Avatar, Prime, and Quintessence. These come from prior to the release of M20.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Avatar background and spending Quintessence</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">All mages may channel at least one Quintessence into their own effects, even if they don't possess the Avatar background trait.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Avatars and Quintessence absorption</b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mages without the Avatar background may still meditate within a Node and gain Quintessence. Mages meditate for one day and then roll for at least one success on a roll of Perception + Meditation, difficulty 9. This gains them a single point of Quintessence per day of quiet reflection.</span></b><br /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Jason, the Storyteller<br /> -<br /> &quot;Old dreams become new again in the spring. This is where the nightmares are.&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1357-storyteller31","name":"Storyteller31","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:21:04-07:00","id":556126,"title":"","content":"Abandoning Instruments:<br /> <br /> When using this house rule, you don't have seven Instruments; you have as many or as few as you like, as long as you have at least one. Instruments don't get set aside individually; instead, they get set aside based on the highest rank required for the Effect:<br /> <br /> \u2022 If a mystic has at least twice as many dots of Arete as the highest Sphere needed for the Effect, he can skip the instruments if he wishes. <br /> \u2022 If a technomancer has at least five more dots of Arete than the highest Sphere needed for the Effect, he can skip the instruments if he wishes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  spelling 06-16-2015, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:38:26-07:00","id":556289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=554908#post554908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought Avatar was too integral as a Background, and encourages min-maxing. I considered having it as a ten-dot Advantage like Arete and Willpower, but realised it would overlap too much with the former. My house rule, then, would be to do away with the Avatar Background altogether and have its mechanics absorbed by Arete. You can channel as many points of Quintessence per turn as you have Arete, then. A simple fix, and a fairer solution, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this as well<br /> <br /> I've been toying with the same idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T16:46:01-07:00","id":557516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=550966#post550966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, IF the Storyteller it's careful on how much Willpower will allow the players to have, it's not bad. Problem with Willpower it's that's a little too cheap (as you start with 5, and one can easily raise it with freebies).<br /> <br /> I think the roll should be Appropriate Attribute + Appropriate Skill (Appropriate being defined by Focus), but that can be somewhat complicated, as needs to be solved in the fly. Willpower it's easier in that sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting points. I would note that the Willpower roll technically can't have specialties, so zeros would never count as 2 successes. (Maybe?) As well - it's for a very specific use - targeting spells, which people already have to sink points into Arete and the Spheres in question. Firearms, Archery don't just let you shoot a weapon, they include maintenance and other technical information.<br /> <br /> Just seemed thematic to me, if Magick is all about focusing Will, then the trait Willpower be used to target spells. I agree that if used this way a ST should be careful - just like with any trait really.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T14:39:54-07:00","id":558764,"title":"","content":"I also think the magick system itself is broken (relatively). Because higher level powers are capped by three factors (obtaining required Sphere level, rolling the higher difficulty and obtaining more successes for a basic effect than for a lower level power), they're always weaker than lower level powers.<br /> <br /> So I'd make the base difficulty of all magick equal to the local Gauntlet or the Willpower of the subject. This makes lower level powers harder, but stops higher level powers seeming relatively low powered in comparison once a person starts gaining Arete.<br /> <br /> I'd require the expenditure of Quintessence for vulgar magic (one point if there are no witnesses, and two points if there are). You might prefer to raise the difficulty by +1 or +2.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'd make more consistent rules for successes, which would take into account the fact Sphere levels already limit Effects.<br /> <br /> If you look at the Magickal Feats chart, for example, you'll note the ascending number of successes roughly mirrors the ascending Sphere levels. In effect, it's not necessary to require five successes for a fifth Sphere level Effect if you're already restricting such Effects to a high level of mastery. To do so is to make level five powers doubly difficult.<br /> <br /> So I'd make one success a basic success for any Effect appropriate to its Sphere prerequisites. <br /> <br /> So a roll for a level five Sphere will achieve a level five Effect with just one success. However, I'd make more concrete rules about allocating successes to duration, range, etc. So you'd still need multiple successes for anything but a fleeting spell, but having a level five Sphere would at least make it easier to create more powerful Effects.<br /> <br /> Does anyone else have any suggestions for fixing the magick rules for higher level Spheres? I'm still looking for a really elegant fix, which must exist somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T14:51:11-07:00","id":558770,"title":"","content":"The simplest fix I can think of, actually, is to put all difficulties at 6 (7 or 8 for vulgar) and ignore Sphere levels. <br /> <br /> Instead, to achieve the more powerful Effects you just need to roll the number of successes on the Magickal Feats chart. You can make this an extended roll, but can only roll a number of times equal to your current Sphere rating in the lowest Sphere used (each failed roll makes the next turn's roll increase by +1 difficulty). Those with lower Sphere levels will still struggle, but everyone has a chance.<br /> <br /> For rotes, which require understanding as much as raw talent, you have to have the relevant Sphere levels, or the action counts as an Effect instead.<br /> <br /> It allows for more flexibility, but the low Arete levels involved stop it from being overpowered at lower levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T19:09:27-07:00","id":558975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=520208#post520208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">House rule I'm using will be aiming the spell with an actual roll like Perception + Occult or such for Fireball and not Arete. Don't know how you dodge a lightning bolt with ease. Either way, makes Forces almost useless in magic since a single success will beat a Mage. That's such a stupid rule, I don't know why they even added it. Not playing NWoD, why am I rolling to do damage and not to hit?<br /> <br /> Better question is how do you DODGE a freaking curse?<br /> <br /> &quot;Well I felt that damn mage tossing a curse at me so I side step it and dodge the thing! Teach that punk nerd to mess with me!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I often don't allow dodging of magic<br /> <br /> I've discussed this often and I feel that to dodge magic may make sense if the character casting magic does so in a way that causes it's target to be aware that magic is going to effect his location<br /> <br /> if a mage creates a ball of fire in his hand and then throws it at me, I know that the mage is throwing a ball of fire at me and I can leap out of the way.<br /> <br /> If a mage tweaks a device or two while looking at her phone and suddenly an electrical storm appears where I stand I don't believe that I should be able to dodge that effect unless I can see the future or sense that I'm in danger by some other means.<br /> <br /> A lot of people who disagree with me say &quot;well maybe the electrical storm was off target&quot;, this argument is naturally irrelevant to many player. As one mage said, &quot;When I do magic, I change reality to be as I WILL it to be&quot;, that doesn't mean the mage can't WILL the electrical storm to be at a certain location with accuracy, the storm will manifest wherever the mage wills it to manifest without fail (as long as the mage can produce that effect).<br /> <br /> Stating that the location where the magic takes effect can not be controlled is no different than saying the time when the magic takes effect or the ultimate form that the magic takes can not be controlled; it makes no sense, it's like saying &quot;you're healing effect 'missed' the NPC so it turned him into a rabbit instead&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, the other perspective is that this overly empowers mages and that it's unfair... but to that I can only say that being a sleeper in a world in which mages walk the earth is indeed unfair","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","user":"Dream_Walker","date":". 06-17-2015, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T09:02:40-07:00","id":559426,"title":"","content":"As Dream_Walker said, there's no need to complicate things too much, but I disagree with the storm being undefendable. If the magick is cast in such away it has to connect, then it has an attack roll and a defense roll can be used to avoid it. If the magick is cast in such a way it just lands, then there's no attack nor defense roll.<br /> &quot;I chant the Names of the Fire Servants to conjure a fireball that speeds towards my enemy&quot;. This dude will roll an attack (most likely dex/athletics) and the other dude can defend.<br /> (arete serves only to calculate damage, attack precision applies)<br /> <br /> &quot;Breathing deep, I channel my chi into my lungs with tainted essence, then breath it out in a cloud of poison&quot;. This dude will roll an attack (most likely stamina/athletics or do) and the targets in the cloud will be able to avoid it or hold their breaths in time.<br /> (arete serves to make an impressive effect, probably damage over time or some debilitation, attack precision does not apply)<br /> <br /> &quot;I release my glass-ether wasps, who fly into the sky and accumulate energy around them to hurl a lightning bolt from above at my enemy.&quot; This dude will roll an attack (most likely int/hypertech) and the other dude can defend. The victim will likely not see it coming though(high above, not visible), and not be eligible to defend. If the victim is aware, however, he'll defend normally. Tricks like this don't tend to work twice on the same target.<br /> (same as fireball)<br /> <br /> &quot;I etch the Rune of Pain deep enough on my skin to draw blood, and smear it on her face to lay a death curse.&quot; This dude will roll an attack (most likely dex/brawl) and the other dude can defend.<br /> (same as poison breath)<br /> <br /> &quot;I scan the target and infect his motion algorithms with my favorite incandescense malware. If he moves, he'll lit up like a bonfire.&quot; This dude will not need to roll an attack, and the other dude can't evade. The fact this particular magick has an &quot;escape&quot; clause (don't move) is particular. Some witch could evil eye someone into a heart attack, for example.<br /> (arete does everything. it's an impressive effect that just hits)<br /> <br /> And, of course, countermagick applies against all cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":".  Formatting and Clarity 06-18-2015, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:03:27-07:00","id":559976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=558770#post558770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simplest fix I can think of, actually, is to put all difficulties at 6 (7 or 8 for vulgar) and ignore Sphere levels.<br /> <br /> Instead, to achieve the more powerful Effects you just need to roll the number of successes on the Magickal Feats chart. You can make this an extended roll, but can only roll a number of times equal to your current Sphere rating in the lowest Sphere used (each failed roll makes the next turn's roll increase by +1 difficulty). Those with lower Sphere levels will still struggle, but everyone has a chance.<br /> <br /> For rotes, which require understanding as much as raw talent, you have to have the relevant Sphere levels, or the action counts as an Effect instead.<br /> <br /> It allows for more flexibility, but the low Arete levels involved stop it from being overpowered at lower levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my plan as well, base difficulty of 5.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T18:22:07-07:00","id":561431,"title":"","content":"In the &quot;violence as a focus&quot; system it seems that, if you use it to deliver a direct damage effect, then the damage of the magick overrides the damage of the weapon.<br /> <br /> This seems odd to me. If you increase the kinetic energy of a bullet, and add Prime to it, (like in the example, in p.563) you're going to cause the same damage than doing the same with a sword or a punch (albeit the punch will need Prime 3 or a glove). Nor to mention that the caliber of the bullet, or the potency of the weapon, are irrelevant to the damage.<br /> <br /> It seems that, when magick it's used, it is literally true that what matters it's not the weapon, but the warrior who uses it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However amusing this oddity may be, it generates certain problems.<br /> <br /> For a thing, it benefits the mages who use less complicated weapons or techniques (that is, weapons or techniques that have an easier difficulty to hit), over big and damaging weapons.<br /> I don't think this it's a good thing. I understand that, in Mage, the &quot;mood&quot; it's more important than the &quot;practicality&quot; , but there is nothing to gain in giving those who use simple punches and kicks a magickal advantage over those who use more complex martial arts techniques. It doesn't benefit the mood...and may bother some players<br /> <br /> Also, in some cases (specialy when using enchanted weapons), it may be that using &quot;violence as a focus&quot; to deliver an extra magic(k)al pain, end causing less damage than would have caused the weapon.<br /> It depends on luck, and on what enhancements has the weapon, but it's an oddity that can happen. For instance, using Forces 2 (without Prime) to enhance the kinetic energy of a katana causes Lethal damage...but, what if the katana was enchanted previously to cause aggravated?. Rules in hand, nor the damage nor the type of the damage, of the weapon apply. <hr />My house rule proposal on this it's the next:<br /> <br /> While using &quot;violence as a focus&quot;, and after delivering the hit with success, and checking for Arete, we must compare the result of the Arete check, with the potential damage of the weapon (like, Strength + 3, for a katana).<br /> If the potential damage of the weapon it's higher than the damage caused by the magick, then we add to the damage a number of damage dice equal to the difference.<br /> <br /> Also, if the spell would cause Contundent or Lethal damage, but the weapon causes a more damaging type of damage, then the type of damage of the weapon may override the damage type of the spell (using Forces 2 to argument the kinetic energy of a katana causes Lethal damage, but if the katana normally caused aggravated...why should cause Lethal when striking whith more force?). Of course, exceptions may arise, dependant on the nature of the magick.<br /> <br /> If the attack roll scored more than one success, the extra successes can be added to the damage, like in revised edition (a good aimed magickal shot may cause more damage than a bad aimed magickal shot).<br /> <br /> If this system seems too dependant on rolls, it may be possible to just sum all the extra damage dice than we've counted, an add half of them (rounded down) as direct damage<br /> <br /> This way, using complex and damaging techniques isn't penalized, and enchanted weapons can still benefit of their magick when used as foucs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-19-2015, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T20:53:18-07:00","id":561532,"title":"","content":"Or you use Action-Enhancing Magick, and make a damage-improving effect instead of a damage effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T03:43:32-07:00","id":561762,"title":"","content":"I'd go with the damage-improving Effect option instead, and add the successes to the damage. It doesn't make sense for a magickal attack with a weapon to do less damage than if magick wasn't used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T04:07:36-07:00","id":561769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=561762#post561762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with the damage-improving Effect option instead, and add the successes to the damage. It doesn't make sense for a magickal attack with a weapon to do less damage than if magick wasn't used.</div> </div> </div> </div>My rule of thumb there (is it canon? I don't remember) is that damage improvement is 1:1 ratio, while normally raw damage is 1:2<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T07:03:34-07:00","id":561868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=561769#post561769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My rule of thumb there (is it canon? I don't remember) is that damage improvement is 1:1 ratio, while normally raw damage is 1:2</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was thinking too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T11:14:56-07:00","id":562097,"title":"","content":"Not only that. Damage improvement gives you some extra <i>damage dice</i>, unlike raw damage, wich are <i>damage levels</i>. A very important distinction.<br /> <br /> That's something that needs to be pondered, I think:<br /> A katana with a +3 (for a total +6) to damage won't likely cause 6 levels of damage, unless your character has Strength 5, and/or, gets<i> extra damage dice from the attack roll</i>. If the bonus and the damage are increased, the difference increases too. (that is, it's less likely to cause 8 levels of damage with a katana+4 (4 Arete successes), than 6 with a katana +3 (3 Arete successes))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-20-2015, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:36:35-07:00","id":563447,"title":"","content":"I'm also pondering the Arete + Sphere hack. Since Spheres are capped by Arete anyway, it just seems like doubling up Arete, and still doesn't make most dice pools much bigger until characters become Masters. <br /> <br /> For a bigger dice pool, Willpower seems like a far more natural solution, and it makes crossovers especially easier. But does that put too much emphasis on Willpower as a trait?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T20:40:29-07:00","id":563691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=563447#post563447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also pondering the Arete + Sphere hack. Since Spheres are capped by Arete anyway, it just seems like doubling up Arete, and still doesn't make most dice pools much bigger until characters become Masters.<br /> <br /> For a bigger dice pool, Willpower seems like a far more natural solution, and it makes crossovers especially easier. But does that put too much emphasis on Willpower as a trait?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quite satisfied with spellcasting rolls being Arete+Avatar (plus everybody has 1 avatar, and avatar is expensive to rise). It's a bit more streamlined, keys part of your spells' power to something the setting does key directly to a mage's power, gives some use to the background besides being a glorified battery, and doesn't change the dynamics of the liminar rules, since they're all still keyed to arete alone (sphere cap, automatic successes...).<br /> <br /> Sticking base difficulties to 6/7/8 instead of Sphere+3/4/5 also works pretty well. The low level loss is compensated by bigger pool, and the high level gain is alleviated by the typical large amounts of successes necessary to cast anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:09:03-07:00","id":564612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=563691#post563691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arete+Avatar</div> </div> </div> </div>Now THAT is an interesting fix that I hadn't considered before. I too have granted my players 1 point in Avatar for free, with the intent to make it about as difficult as Arete to raise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T17:29:57-07:00","id":564774,"title":"","content":"I considered Arete + Avatar, but it would just encourage players to throw all their points into what is a very cheap trait in M20 (for five of their seven Background dots, they'd get a minimum casting pool of 6 dice and would be able to channel five dots of Quintessence per turn). I've also scrapped the Avatar trait and rolled it into Arete already for this same reason. <br /> <br /> I think I'm going to go with Attribute + Sphere (similar to Changeling, which I play more often), because it encourages players to invest in a wider range of traits. Plus, Spheres seem kinda analogous to Abilities, so it fits the (initial) simplicity that the Storyteller system presents.<br /> <br /> I'm also rolling Resonance into Echoes (or, rather, requiring people with Echoes to flesh those Echoes out as per the Resonance sidebar), as M20 gives descriptions for it but doesn't say how a character generates, gains or loses Resonance dots. I can't find any mechanical stuff for Synergy, either, beyond the fact it's Dynamic, Static or Entropic. I'm guessing maybe the ST just allocates a rating to places and locations, and then narrates how this might affect or colour a mage's magick? I searched the entire book for better crunch here, but just found an annoying reference to the next supplement. (Am I missing something?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:28:54-07:00","id":565382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=564774#post564774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered Arete + Avatar, but it would just encourage players to throw all their points into what is a very cheap trait in M20</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why Avatar is repriced when that happens. It's probably best put just behind arete in cost to buy/upgrade<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T08:27:46-07:00","id":565435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'm going to go with Attribute + Sphere (similar to Changeling, which I play more often), because it encourages players to invest in a wider range of traits. Plus, Spheres seem kinda analogous to Abilities, so it fits the (initial) simplicity that the Storyteller system presents.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do so, then what role will serve Arete beyond 5 in your game? (assuming you're going to use it). <hr />I was thinking on my &quot;supernatural counterspelling&quot; problem. What if instead of making the difficulty of said counterspelling 6 or Arete (whichever its higher, as per the rules), we limit it to the permanent Willpower of the mage.<br /> <br /> The old Thaumaturgy counterspelling system used Willpower as it's difficulty (it's a classic). Also since such a Trait it's easier to get than Arete 7+, then the raise in difficulty that supernaturals seem to experiment when facing some mages (in particular, powerful ones) wouldn't be anecdotal (powerful mages tend to have bigger Willpower, anyway)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T11:47:58-07:00","id":565600,"title":"","content":"The main problem I have, especially with younger players, is that the moment they see that they &quot;only&quot; have one, two or three dice at the beginning to do magic they loose all their motivation. Seriously, it's like watching a balloon loose it's air. I don't know if we have some kind of deep bias that we need as many dice as possible but that's how they feel. Even after I explain to them that mage is not a game about power but extraordinary people and what they do to change the world, even after I tell them that they have options like using quintaessence and willpower it's useless. Anyone here with this problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 06-23-2015, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:05:05-07:00","id":565682,"title":"","content":"I've seen it happen.<br /> <br /> IME it's a result of the flexibility of the magic system combined with how powerful even a single success can really be. A lot of players new to Mage really don't know how to calibrate their expectations. When most of the system treats 3 successes as a &quot;basic&quot; success, only have 1-3 dice seems like you'll almost never get what you want with magic without throwing every last modifier and a WP at it.<br /> <br /> The system itself sets the bias that you usually need ~6 dice to be considered good at something, but then shoves magic to such a low starting dice-pool. Besides house rules to increase the dice-pool in some fashion, the only way I've been able to get players past that is by talking them into playing long enough to try things out and then get the hang of it; at which point such concerns usually stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T14:17:09-07:00","id":565752,"title":"","content":"Well, an improvement from M20 when compared with revised edition is that you don't need as many successes, since you don't need to divide dice. <br /> <br /> One problem is when the subject can null your powers in a one by one basis with a dicepool that it's much larger than yours (like Willpower. That's why mind magicks need to be very subtle, or very powerful)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T05:16:08-07:00","id":575064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=565435#post565435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you do so, then what role will serve Arete beyond 5 in your game? (assuming you're going to use it).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably unlikely to happen for most characters, but the fact that the caps on Spheres goes up too makes up for this. At Arete 6, characters can raise their Spheres to 6 too, which will be reflected in their dice pool (Attribute + Sphere).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if we decide to avoid Archspheres altogether (easier, TBH), I might translate the extra dots of Arete over 5 into automatic successes or a reduction in difficulty/threshold. Probably the former. That still encourages players to invest in Arete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T15:52:20-07:00","id":576840,"title":"","content":"Has anyone come up with paradox rules that are more varied than the &quot;one point for all things vulgar&quot; rule.<br /> <br /> I threw down on that and would like to hear what other's have done.<br /> <br /> It just doesn't make sense to me to get one point of dox whether I summon a candle flame or summon a giant spider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T16:29:22-07:00","id":576879,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you might want to tie the amount of Paradox generated to the number of successes achieved on a Vulgar effect \u2014 say, one Paradox for every five successes (or fraction thereof) needed to achieve the feat. Most Feats would still be one Paradox each; but Mighty Feats would tend to generate two Paradox, Outlandish Feats would tend to generate three or four, and Godlike Feats would tend to generate five or more. <br /> <br /> I've also toyed with the notion of Vulgar effects generating 1 Paradox, plus one more Paradox for every &quot;1&quot; rolled, regardless of how many successes are rolled. This results in larger dice pools and extended rolls generating more Paradox, at an average rate of one more Paradox for every ten dice rolled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T22:25:22-07:00","id":577087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=576879#post576879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like you might want to tie the amount of Paradox generated to the number of successes achieved on a Vulgar effect \u2014 say, one Paradox for every five successes (or fraction thereof) needed to achieve the feat. Most Feats would still be one Paradox each; but Mighty Feats would tend to generate two Paradox, Outlandish Feats would tend to generate three or four, and Godlike Feats would tend to generate five or more.<br /> <br /> I've also toyed with the notion of Vulgar effects generating 1 Paradox, plus one more Paradox for every &quot;1&quot; rolled, regardless of how many successes are rolled. This results in larger dice pools and extended rolls generating more Paradox, at an average rate of one more Paradox for every ten dice rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>It already happens, considering you'll need extended effects to pull so many successes, and extended magicks <b>already</b> accrue more paradox: None if coincident, [number of rolls] if vulgar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T06:31:23-07:00","id":577298,"title":"","content":"Not really, as I have said, that Paradox exist only in a botch. The idea that you indeed garner it, but discharge harmlessly in a success it's purely academic, the Paradox isn't here if you don't suffer it.<br /> <br /> Now, the normal rules are a sort of Damocles Sword. You CAN get out with a lot. If lucky, Your mage can change reality in very noticeable ways, and cast down mighty magicks. Of course, someday, you won't be lucky (and there's more chances if you need to accrue more successes), and the hammer will fall.<br /> <br /> In contrast, giving a &quot;fixed&quot; number of 'dox, even in a success, makes bigger magicks inherently more paradoxical. So, getting 10 actions per turn whit a Time ritual WILL have more consequences than a 3 successes spell. Actual consequences, not potential ones.<br /> <br /> That's the difference. I personally think that the damocles sword it's more &quot;Mage&quot; than the direct punishment (which, in turn, it's more akin to revised theme of magic dying, and a harsher reality where big miracles can't be). Paradox was always worse in a botch. That says something about the themes of mage.<br /> Hubris is evident when, and only when, your character HAS the power of doing what she wants. That's the moment when a mage, knowing that her magicks might produce a lot of damage, will use them anyway, in the hope that they will succeed. But where they to fail, you will fall from your tower of successes, hard. Well, that's the theorie...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-03-2015, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T07:29:14-07:00","id":577323,"title":"","content":"This is one of the reasons I always applied paradox to each roll for vulgar effects. Bigger change bigger paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T12:30:26-07:00","id":577599,"title":"","content":"The ones im implementing for now are <br /> <br /> Not botching on spellcasting rolls. I mean my games never go past arete 5 really and until they reach that point players are rolling 2 dices for long months until they reach arete 3. So to add to that puny roll the posibiliy of botching is to much IMO<br /> <br /> Secondly i will do away with the familiar rules in favor of the ones in forged by dragon fire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Im curious though, i suggested the idea to my group of doing &quot;arete + sphere&quot; for the spellcasting rolls and they say they didnt want it that because magic became too powerful but i see it as a common houserule, People that have used it, whats have being your experience with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T21:21:10-07:00","id":925689,"title":"","content":"Is there a thread that has house rules that isn't specific to M20? I swear I've seen one, but I can't find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T09:39:28-07:00","id":1125937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=925689#post925689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a thread that has house rules that isn't specific to M20? I swear I've seen one, but I can't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There may be an old thread in the early days on the forum here about House Rules for M:tA, not M20. Not that I can find it either, but I remember something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T14:59:44-08:00","id":1172758,"title":"","content":"Simple House Rule: restore MRev's version of the Blessing Background as a Mystical version of the technomantic Enhancement Background. Since M20 has its own Blessing Background, call it the Gifted Background. It can represent such things as mystical tattoos, psychic powers, or cases where the character has become a Relic (see Book of Secrets).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T15:37:20-08:00","id":1172773,"title":"","content":"Beginning Mage characters, for all their reality warping skill, often feel like that 1st level D&amp;D wizard hoping his single cast of Magic Missile will do the trick. Therefore, the next time I run a Mage game, I'm giving each character a knack, some ability they can perform that wouldn't normally be available at their starting Arete and Sphere level. If the knack is limited in application (I can grow wings and fly!), then I'd allow +2 to the Sphere rating in order to meet its requirement. If the knack is broader (I can manipulate my appendages in all manner of ways) then the PC would need to be within 1 dot of the necessary Sphere.<br /> <br /> This wouldn't be without danger, of course. The PC's Arete doesn't increase for the purpose of casting this spell. Eventually, Sphere and Arete level would reach the point where the knack is just another rote. In that case, I'll give it a bonus to casting of some sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T04:06:58-08:00","id":1172963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Otto D'Fey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=1172773#post1172773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beginning Mage characters, for all their reality warping skill, often feel like that 1st level D&amp;D wizard hoping his single cast of Magic Missile will do the trick. Therefore, the next time I run a Mage game, I'm giving each character a knack, some ability they can perform that wouldn't normally be available at their starting Arete and Sphere level. If the knack is limited in application (I can grow wings and fly!), then I'd allow +2 to the Sphere rating in order to meet its requirement. If the knack is broader (I can manipulate my appendages in all manner of ways) then the PC would need to be within 1 dot of the necessary Sphere.<br /> <br /> This wouldn't be without danger, of course. The PC's Arete doesn't increase for the purpose of casting this spell. Eventually, Sphere and Arete level would reach the point where the knack is just another rote. In that case, I'll give it a bonus to casting of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the fact that this would undercut gaining things like Wonders or other Merits (like, just as one example, Parlor Trick), I think the idea would work at cross purposes to the tone Mage: The Ascension is going for. Everything is supposed to be subtle, and magick is something characters go to great lengths to learn. It's supposed to be a world where magick is rare, because it's (supposedly) dying out. Because of this, every successful act of True Magick represents a major accomplishment.<br /> <br /> In DnD, being able to cast Magic Missile is elementary, because Dungeons and Dragons is a High Fantasy game. Mage: The Ascension wants you to remember that even small feats of Reality-breaking are wondrous and palpable, and should be treasured.<br /> <br /> Making everything based on Arete rolls - which start at low dice pools - also incentivises the sort of prolonged rituals and major build projects that typify Real Life mystic practices and scientific invention. If a character wants to inflict a curse on someone from a distance, they are well served to make a big deal out of the act of laying that curse. As well as going to the trouble of ensuring they have as many advantages working in their favor (to give them as many difficulty breaks as possible).<br /> <br /> Letting you just DO an Effect at the word &quot;Go&quot;, above and beyond what they can normally do, sounds like it would turn into a crutch for players. Why would they go to the effort of crafting a spell tailored to their situation, or work for a great ritual, when they can just rely on their Knack? If a character can just grow wings and fly, why tackle 90% of their problems any other way? They can fly. Flight doesn't solve all problems, certainly, but it's easy for a player to get trapped in the &quot;If all you have is a hammer&quot; mindset, and spam their flight ability for as many problems as they can get away with. It's the most potent tool they'll have for a while.<br /> <br /> All of this, of course, ignoring Paradox. That's an entire other kettle of fish, and one I don't feel like tackling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T10:20:23-08:00","id":1173030,"title":"","content":"I'd also worry about potentially giving players access to Master level effects like that. Being able to, say, Nullify Paradox at start for free on top of having Prime 3 seems like it would really skew with the game.<br /> <br /> The Attainments system from Awakening 2e always seemed like a better idea to port to Ascension for this kind of house rule. Rather than effects they couldn't normally cast, they'd be effects they can cast but with some bonus factors without needing to assign successes, or eliminating the need for a low level conjunctional Sphere, or removing the risk of Paradox but capping how powerful the successes you can get below your max; trading safety for weaker spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:57:50-08:00","id":1173316,"title":"","content":"I would strongly recommend to change the knack to bonus dice (1 or 2).<br /> That way they can't accomplish more, but they feel they have a knack for their thing. Sorta like a speciality is handled in M20.<br /> Powerful stuff gets 1 die (Fire, damage/healing and the likes) more toned down knacks receive 2 dice (sensing stuff, alterations and such things).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T14:38:08-08:00","id":1173332,"title":"","content":"A couple things to note. The Knack isn't a gimme. It's a regular spell vulnerable to Paradox and the necessity of casting with a limited Arete dice pool. They will also be limited in scope, likely tied to events during character Awakening (thus things like Nullify Paradox won't be a part of it--my players know how much I adore Paradox). I've run a <i>lot</i> of Mage over the last 20+ years or so and enjoy trying new things. I also trust my players to look for something very character appropriate rather than OP outlandishness. I'm pretty sure it'll work out just fine; at the very least, it will be an interesting experiment. Assuming we ever get to start that new chronicle, in the face of so many other games we want to play around with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T08:08:20-07:00","id":1459309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Otto D'Fey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=1172773#post1172773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beginning Mage characters, for all their reality warping skill, often feel like that 1st level D&amp;D wizard hoping his single cast of Magic Missile will do the trick. Therefore, the next time I run a Mage game, I'm giving each character a knack, some ability they can perform that wouldn't normally be available at their starting Arete and Sphere level. If the knack is limited in application (I can grow wings and fly!), then I'd allow +2 to the Sphere rating in order to meet its requirement. If the knack is broader (I can manipulate my appendages in all manner of ways) then the PC would need to be within 1 dot of the necessary Sphere.<br /> <br /> This wouldn't be without danger, of course. The PC's Arete doesn't increase for the purpose of casting this spell. Eventually, Sphere and Arete level would reach the point where the knack is just another rote. In that case, I'll give it a bonus to casting of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My thought is you could give the PC's free dots in the Blessing background, as something they &quot;naturally&quot; can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T08:39:18-07:00","id":1459312,"title":"","content":"Note that that only works in MRev. Before that, there was no Blessing Background; and M20 rewrote Blessing into something fundamentally different. The nearest thing that M20 has to MRev's Blessing is Enhancement; and that's Technocrats-only. <br /> <br /> Which is ironic, because MRev's Blessing was supposed to be the mystic counterpart to Enhancement. So my proposed fix is to just expand the types of Enhancements that are allowed to include some that are suitable for mystical Foci, such as enchanted tattoos or blessings designed to empower. <br /> <br /> Another option to consider, though, would be Charles Siegel's Rotes, found in the appendix to his STV supplement <b>Enlightened Grimoire</b>. If you want it to be available without meeting the Arete or Sphere requirements, he addresses that in <b>Sorcerer: Paths of Power</b> with the Rote Sorcerer Merit (p.67).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T02:38:16-07:00","id":1460196,"title":"","content":"Conjunctional Magick does not require casters to have any dots in the Spheres used by other participants. They cast as if they were a single Mage with Arete based on the average of all participants. They take on a Fused status, during which they cannot do individual casting as normal, making them more vulnerable. The Fused status lasts for three times as long as it takes to do the spell. Quiet can spread from a single participant to others. Intense Resonance can spread from one Mage to another while Fused. So, Conjunctional Magick isn't something you would want to do very often, but players can spend precious XP on the Sphere ranks they want to take, rather than spreading it across the bottom. <br /> <br /> Paradox erases the memory of sleepers who witness Vulgar Magick, with some exceptions. Similar to Awakening.<br /> <br /> The number of witnesses to Vulgar Magick affects the amount of Paradox the caster gets and how much of it discharges immediately, the severity of the form the discharge takes.<br /> <br /> As long as a Mage character hasn't completely dismissed the most recent Seeking assigned by their Avatar, the Avatar can manifest as a counteracting influence when the character is targeted by Mind effects that would lead them to corruption or demise. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T04:13:04-07:00","id":1460200,"title":"","content":"The only one of those that I have a problem with is the Fused state lasting beyond the time it takes to do the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T04:41:10-07:00","id":1460203,"title":"","content":"I can see the point to making group casting more prohibitive... it's an extremely potent thing if you can get the right group of mages together.<br /> <br /> But don't expect to see people build &quot;tall&quot; instead of &quot;wide&quot; mages regarding Sphere selections on that alone. The game heavily incentivizes having at least 1 if not 2 or 3 dots in most Spheres in enough ways that you'd need to house rule a lot more than this to get the desired effect (though Awakening is a good resource for what to do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T04:59:09-07:00","id":1460205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=1460200#post1460200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only one of those that I have a problem with is the Fused state lasting beyond the time it takes to do the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe just a high Willpower cost. I want my players thinking mostly about what they alone can do with Magick, Conjunctional Magick being an infrequent but significant event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T05:24:21-07:00","id":1460208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=1460203#post1460203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the point to making group casting more prohibitive... it's an extremely potent thing if you can get the right group of mages together.<br /> <br /> But don't expect to see people build &amp;quot;tall&amp;quot; instead of &amp;quot;wide&amp;quot; mages regarding Sphere selections on that alone. The game heavily incentivizes having at least 1 if not 2 or 3 dots in most Spheres in enough ways that you'd need to house rule a lot more than this to get the desired effect (though Awakening is a good resource for what to do).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Even though Awakening has gone its own way since, especially in 2e, it <i>was</i> originally created by the former MRev development team as \u201cwhat we wish we could have done with Ascension but couldn't because so much was already established before us\u201d. With that in mind, borrowing from Awakening is a fertile source of potential M20 House Rules \u2014 and dare I say, something that I'd encourage the M5 developers to look at, too. A big difference between the two gamelines is how Awakening tries to make the Conjunctional use of Arcana the exception rather than the rule and that's something that I'd very much like to see \u201cbackported\u201d into Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T05:41:17-07:00","id":1460209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/520134-m20-house-rules?p=1460205#post1460205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe just a high Willpower cost. I want my players thinking mostly about what they alone can do with Magick, Conjunctional Magick being an infrequent but significant event.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I prefer this to be a Focus driven choice, with some approaches to Magick trending toward the solitary workings while others prefer cooperative castings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=